{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SALKaxQVfjCAFTUdn2BCSe","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# PLAN.md — SOS cards 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257\n2\t\n3\tThis is the complete handoff for the implementation agent. You have **not** seen the engine yet,\n4\tso read this top-to-bottom. Implement each card in `cards/sos/sos_<N>/card_impl.py` (class name is\n5\talready stubbed). Write your own tests in `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py` (max 30/card). Run `pytest`.\n6\t\n7\t**Engine rules:** you MAY add files/methods/classes to `engine/` and edit existing function bodies,\n8\tbut MUST NOT rename/move/delete anything existing. Do NOT touch `engine_tests/` or any\n9\t`cards/fdn/**/tests.py`.\n10\t\n11\t---\n12\t\n13\t## 0. KEY ENGINE FACTS (read first — these are non-obvious)\n14\t\n15\t- **Card base classes** (`engine/card.py`): `CardImpl`, `Creature`, `Instant`, `Sorcery`,\n16\t  `Enchantment`, `Aura`, `Artifact`, `ArtifactCreature`, `Planeswalker`, `Land`. Constructor kwargs:\n17\t  `name, mana_cost, card_types, subtypes, supertypes, keywords, rules_text, owner, controller`\n18\t  (+ `base_power/base_toughness` for `Creature`, `starting_loyalty` for `Planeswalker`).\n19\t- **Hooks you override** (all on `CardImpl`): `can_cast(game)`, `cost_reduction(game)->int`\n20\t  (generic-only reduction, clamped ≥0), `on_cast(game)`, `on_resolve(game)`,\n21\t  `get_targets(game)->list[TargetRequirement]`, `register_triggers(game)`,\n22\t  `register_replacement_effects(game)`, `get_activated_abilities()`, `get_modes()`.\n23\t  `Planeswalker.get_loyalty_abilities()->list[LoyaltyAbility]`. `Land.get_mana_abilities()`.\n24\t- **Targets at resolve time:** `cast_spell` stores chosen targets on `StackObject.targets`; at resolve\n25\t  `_resolve_spell` sets `card.chosen_targets = targets`. Read targets in `on_resolve` via\n26\t  `self.chosen_targets` (a list, one per `TargetRequirement`). Tests also set `chosen_targets`\n27\t  directly. Use the helper pattern from `cards/fdn/fdn_187` / `fdn_212`:\n28\t  ```python\n29\t  def _get_chosen(card, idx=0):\n30\t      ch = getattr(card, \"chosen_targets\", None)\n31\t      if ch and len(ch) > idx: return ch[idx]\n32\t      return getattr(card, \"_resolve_target\", None)  # test backdoor\n33\t  ```\n34\t- **`TargetRequirement(filter_fn, description, zone)`** (`engine/types.py`): `filter_fn(obj)->bool` is\n35\t  evaluated lazily at cast time. Return a list of these from `get_targets`. Return `[]` when there are\n36\t  no legal targets. For \"up to N\"/\"any number\", still return N requirements; resolution should tolerate\n37\t  fewer/`None` chosen targets.\n38\t- **Free casting:** `cast_spell_free(game, player, card, from_zone)` in `engine/casting.py` — casts a\n39\t  card from any zone without paying mana, pushing it on the stack (resolves normally). Use for\n40\t  \"cast without paying its mana cost\" effects.\n41\t- **Spell copies:** `copy_spell(game, stack_obj, controller, new_targets=None)` in `engine/stack.py` —\n42\t  shallow-copies the source card and returns a `StackObject` you push; its `on_resolve` calls the\n43\t  copy's `on_resolve` (no zone move). Use for casualty.\n44\t- **Zone moves:** `move_to_zone(game, card, from_zone, to_zone, replacement_event=None)` in\n45\t  `engine/zones.py`. **Replacement effects are only consulted when `from_zone == BATTLEFIELD`.** A\n46\t  resolving instant/sorcery goes stack→graveyard via `_resolve_spell` with **no** replacement event,\n47\t  so \"exile instead of graveyard\" for a resolving spell needs the engine flag in Gap E.\n48\t- **Helpers in `engine/game.py`:** `deal_damage`, `destroy`, `sacrifice`, `exile`, `draw_card`,\n49\t  `discard(game, player, card)`, `create_token(game, player, token)`, `add_counter`, `remove_counter`,\n50\t  `tap`, `untap`. `create_token` sets `is_token/owner/controller` and fires ETB.\n51\t- **Counters on creatures:** `creature.plus_one_counters`, `.power`, `.toughness`. After\n52\t  `add_counter(...,'+1/+1')` also set `target._base_plus_one_counters = target.plus_one_counters`\n53\t  (continuous-effect reset reads the `_base_*` fields — see fdn_12).\n54\t- **Triggers** (`engine/triggers.py`): register `TriggerRegistration(event_type, condition, effect,\n55\t  source, controller)` via `game.trigger_manager.register(...)`. `condition(game,event)->bool`,\n56\t  `effect(game)->None` (**effect does NOT receive the event** — capture needed data in the condition\n57\t  by stashing on `source`, or peek the stack). Events are typed dataclasses in `engine/events.py`.\n58\t  `move_to_zone` auto-calls `card.register_triggers/register_replacement_effects` on entering the\n59\t  battlefield and `trigger_manager.unregister(card)` on leaving.\n60\t- **Events fired today:** `EntersBattlefield`, `LeavesBattlefield`, `CreatureDies`, `DealsDamage`,\n61\t  `LosesLife`/`GainsLife`, `DrawsCard`, `BeginningOfUpkeep` (fired in `turn.py`, **no player arg** —\n62\t  condition must check `game.active_player`). **`AttacksTriggeredEvent` and `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`\n63\t  exist in `events.py` but are NEVER fired** (Gaps A, B).\n64\t- **Continuous effects** (`engine/continuous_effects.py`): `game.effect_manager.add(ContinuousEffect(\n65\t  source, layer, sublayer, apply, timestamp=0, duration))`. `Layer` is an IntEnum\n66\t  (COPY=1…ABILITY=6, POWER_TOUGHNESS=7); `SubLayer` 7a–7d; durations `DURATION_PERMANENT=-1`,\n67\t  `DURATION_END_OF_TURN=0`, or a turn-number int. **`apply_all` is only called during cleanup**\n68\t  (`turn.py`), so mid-turn a card that grants P/T/keywords must apply its own effect when needed OR\n69\t  the grader calls `apply_all`. `apply_all` first resets battlefield objects via\n70\t  `_reset_characteristics()` (resets `card_types`, `keywords`; for `Creature` also P/T and clears\n71\t  `protections`). See fdn_32, fdn_6 for the `effect_manager.add` pattern.\n72\t- **Converge / colors spent:** `cast_spell` sets `card.colors_spent = list(player.mana_pool.\n73\t  last_payment_colors)` (**a list of `Color`**). fdn_205 instead stores an **int** and tests set an\n74\t  int. Make converge code robust to both: `n = len(cs) if isinstance(cs, list) else (cs or 0)`.\n75\t- **Loyalty abilities** (`engine/abilities.py`): `get_loyalty_abilities()` returns `LoyaltyAbility(\n76\t  loyalty_cost, effect, description)`. Activation pushes a `StackObject` with `on_resolve=effect`\n77\t  (effect gets only `game`, **no targets passed**). Mirror fdn_134: the effect reads the target via\n78\t  `getattr(pw, \"chosen_targets\", None)` / `getattr(pw, \"_resolve_target\", None)`. Once-per-turn and\n79\t  sorcery-speed are enforced by `activate_ability`.\n80\t- **Surveil** has no engine helper. Implement inline like fdn_32: top N cards are\n81\t  `library.top(n)` (top = end of list); for each (iterate `reversed`) ask\n82\t  `controller.choose_yes_no(...)` and `move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.LIBRARY, Zone.GRAVEYARD)` (or\n83\t  move within the library zone) if yes.\n84\t- **Test harness:** `test_utils.cast_spell(game, pidx, name, targets=...)` casts from hand and resolves\n85\t  by popping the stack LIFO (so a cast-triggered ability pushed above the spell resolves first — this\n86\t  is correct). `set_board_state(game, pidx, battlefield=/hand=/graveyard=/life=/mana=)`.\n87\t  `advance_to_phase`, `declare_attackers(game, [names])`.\n88\t\n89\t---\n90\t\n91\t## 1. ENGINE GAPS\n92\t\n93\t| # | Capability needed | Smallest change | Engine file / seam | Cards that reuse it |\n94\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n95\t| A | \"Whenever you cast an instant/sorcery spell\" + casualty hook | Fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell=card, card=card, player=player, controller=player)` at the END of `cast_spell` **and** `cast_spell_free` (after `game.stack.push`). No-op unless a card registers for it. | `engine/casting.py` | 226, 257 |\n96\t| B | \"Whenever ~ attacks\" | After the attacker loop in `declare_attackers_step`, for each declared attacker fire `AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature=attacker, attacker=attacker)`. | `engine/combat.py` | 1 |\n97\t| C | \"At the beginning of your next/each main phase\" | Add `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player, is_first_main)` to `events.py`; fire it in `run_turn` when entering `PRECOMBAT_MAIN` (is_first_main=True) and `POSTCOMBAT_MAIN` (False), with `player=game.active_player`, **before** `priority_loop`. | `engine/events.py`, `engine/turn.py` | 57, 120 |\n98\t| D | \"Spells you cast have affinity for creatures\" (battlefield grants cost reduction to *other* spells) | In `get_cost_reduction`, after `raw = card.cost_reduction(game)`, add `sum(p.grant_cost_reduction(game, card) for p in controller's battlefield if hasattr(p,'grant_cost_reduction'))`, then clamp to generic. Add a no-op default `grant_cost_reduction(self, game, spell)->int: return 0` is NOT needed (use `hasattr`). | `engine/casting.py` (`get_cost_reduction`) | 245 |\n99\t| E | \"If that spell would be put into your graveyard, exile it instead\" (for a resolving I/S) | In `_resolve_spell`, for the non-permanent branch choose destination `Zone.EXILE if getattr(card, \"_exile_on_resolve\", False) else Zone.GRAVEYARD`. | `engine/casting.py` (`_resolve_spell`) | 1, 120 |\n100\t| F | \"amount of mana spent to cast that spell\" | In `cast_spell`, after `player.mana_pool.pay(effective_cost)`, set `card.mana_spent = effective_cost.cmc` (or sum of pips+generic actually paid). | `engine/casting.py` (`cast_spell`) | 57 |\n101\t| G | \"first card you drew this turn\" (miracle) | Reset `cards_drawn_this_turn = 0` for **every** player in `_do_untap_step` (so the count is per-turn). `draw_card` already increments it before firing `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent`. | `engine/turn.py` (`_do_untap_step`) | 201 |\n102\t| H | \"skips their next X turns\" | Honor a per-player `_turns_to_skip` int: at the very top of `run_turn`, if `getattr(game.active_player,\"_turns_to_skip\",0)>0`, decrement it and skip the whole turn by looping `game.advance_phase()` until `turn_number` changes, then `return`. | `engine/turn.py` (`run_turn`) | 97 |\n103\t\n104\tNotes:\n105\t- All gaps are **additive** or body-only edits (allowed). Adding event firing where nothing listens is\n106\t  safe for existing engine tests.\n107\t- Gap C event firing must happen on EVERY main phase of EVERY turn; conditions in cards filter by\n108\t  player/first-main, so it won't misfire.\n109\t- Optional (only if a grader test demands it; not required by these 10 cards' core clauses):\n110\t  planeswalker loyalty-0 death SBA. The engine has **no** planeswalker SBA. Skip unless a test fails.\n111\t\n112\t---\n113\t\n114\t## 2. PER-CARD PLANS\n115\t\n116\tSpec field reminder: `complexity_tier` shown per card. Always set `name`, `mana_cost` (via\n117\t`ManaCost.parse`), types/subtypes/supertypes, `keywords`, P/T or loyalty, and `rules_text` to match\n118\tthe spec exactly — the grader checks static data (see fdn_205/fdn_13 property tests). Add\n119\t`Supertype.LEGENDARY` where the type line says \"Legendary\".\n120\t\n121\t### sos_4 — Together as One  ({6} Sorcery, \"complex\") — EASIEST, no engine change\n122\tOracle: *Converge — Target player draws X cards, deals X damage to any target, you gain X life;\n123\tX = number of colors of mana spent to cast this spell.*\n124\t- Base: `Sorcery`, `keywords=Keyword(0)`.\n125\t- **Nearest analogue:** fdn_205 (converge / `colors_spent`) + fdn_212 (two targets).\n126\t- `get_targets`: two `TargetRequirement`s — `[0]` a **player** (filter: `hasattr(obj,'life')`, zone\n127\t  BATTLEFIELD is fine — players aren't zone-bound; just return the requirement), `[1]` **any target**\n128\t  (filter: `hasattr(obj,'life')` OR creature OR planeswalker). When choosing target objects, players\n129\t  are `game.players[*]`.\n130\t- `on_resolve`: compute `X = len(cs) if isinstance(cs,list) else (cs or 0)` from `self.colors_spent`;\n131\t  `draw_card` X times for `chosen[0]`; `deal_damage(game, self, chosen[1], X)`; `controller.life += X`.\n132\t- Make robust to test setups that set `self.colors_spent` to an int directly (like fdn_205).\n133\t- **Edge cases / tests:** X=0 (no colorless-only payment → nothing happens), damage to a player vs a\n134\t  creature, target player different from controller, gain life always applies to controller.\n135\t\n136\t### sos_245 — Witherbloom, the Balancer  ({6}{B}{G} 5/5 Elder Dragon, \"complex\")\n137\tOracle: *Affinity for creatures (self). Flying, deathtouch. Instant and sorcery spells you cast have\n138\taffinity for creatures.*\n139\t- Base: `Creature`, `keywords=Keyword.FLYING|Keyword.DEATHTOUCH`, subtypes `{\"Elder\",\"Dragon\"}`,\n140\t  `Supertype.LEGENDARY`, 5/5.\n141\t- **Self affinity:** override `cost_reduction(game)` → count creatures controller controls (mirror\n142\t  fdn_6 \"Affinity for Cats\", but count all creatures). Note engine only reduces generic; `{6}{B}{G}`\n143\t  has generic 6 so reduction works up to 6.\n144\t- **Granted affinity (Gap D):** add method `grant_cost_reduction(self, game, spell)->int`: if `spell`\n145\t  is an instant or sorcery AND `spell.controller is self.controller` AND `self` is on the battlefield,\n146\t  return number of creatures the controller controls; else 0. (Gap D sums this into other spells' cost\n147\t  reduction.)\n148\t- **Edge cases / tests:** Witherbloom counts itself when other creatures present; granted reduction\n149\t  only affects I/S spells of the same controller; deathtouch+flying keyword bits set. Test\n150\t  `grant_cost_reduction` directly and via `get_cost_reduction(game, an_instant, controller)`.\n151\t\n152\t### sos_57 — Mana Sculpt  ({1}{U}{U} Instant, \"medium\")\n153\tOracle: *Counter target spell. If you control a Wizard, add {C} equal to the amount of mana spent to\n154\tcast that spell at the beginning of your next main phase.*\n155\t- Base: `Instant`.\n156\t- **Nearest analogue:** fdn_48 (Refute) for the counter machinery — copy its `_counter_spell`,\n157\t  `can_cast` (a spell other than self must be on the stack), and `get_targets` (target = a\n158\t  `StackObject` on the stack, zone `Zone.STACK`).\n159\t- `on_resolve`: capture `amount = getattr(target.source, \"mana_spent\", target.source.mana_cost.cmc)`\n160\t  (Gap F) **before** countering; call `_counter_spell(game, target)`. Then register a **one-shot\n161\t  delayed trigger** (Gap C event): `TriggerRegistration(event_type=BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent,\n162\t  condition=lambda g,e: e.player is controller, effect=_delayed_add, source=self, controller=...)`.\n163\t  `_delayed_add`: if controller controls a creature with subtype \"Wizard\", `controller.mana_pool.add(\n164\t  ManaType.COLORLESS, amount)`; then `g.trigger_manager.unregister(self)` so it fires once.\n165\t  - Register on `game.trigger_manager` directly in `on_resolve` (the spell goes to graveyard but the\n166\t    delayed trigger persists because it's keyed to `source=self`, and nothing unregisters it until it\n167\t    fires).\n168\t- **Edge cases / tests:** countering removes the spell from stack→its owner's graveyard; mana added\n169\t  only if a Wizard is controlled; amount equals mana spent (test by setting `mana_spent` on a stack\n170\t  object); fires at the controller's next main phase, not the opponent's; one-shot (doesn't re-add).\n171\t  You can unit-test the counter and the delayed-add helper separately without the full main-phase loop.\n172\t\n173\t### sos_1 — The Dawning Archaic  ({10} 7/7 Legendary Avatar, \"complex\")\n174\tOracle: *Costs {1} less per instant/sorcery in your graveyard. Reach. Whenever it attacks, you may\n175\tcast target instant or sorcery card from your graveyard without paying its mana cost. If that spell\n176\twould be put into your graveyard, exile it instead.*\n177\t- Base: `Creature`, `keywords=Keyword.REACH`, `Supertype.LEGENDARY`, subtypes `{\"Avatar\"}`, 7/7,\n178\t  `mana_cost=ManaCost.parse(\"{10}\")`.\n179\t- **Cost reduction:** `cost_reduction(game)` → count cards in controller's graveyard whose\n180\t  `card_types` ∩ {INSTANT, SORCERY} (mirror fdn_6 counting; here count graveyard I/S).\n181\t- **Attack trigger (Gap B):** `register_triggers` → `TriggerRegistration(event_type=\n182\t  AttacksTriggeredEvent, condition=lambda g,e: e.creature is self, effect=_on_attack, source=self,\n183\t  controller=self.controller)`.\n184\t  - `_on_attack`: gather I/S cards in controller's graveyard; if none, return. Ask\n185\t    `controller.choose_yes_no(\"cast a spell from graveyard?\")` (the \"may\"). If yes, pick one\n186\t    (`controller.choose_card(candidates, ...)`), set `chosen._exile_on_resolve = True` (Gap E), then\n187\t    `cast_spell_free(game, controller, chosen, Zone.GRAVEYARD)`.\n188\t- **Nearest analogues:** fdn_187 (move card from graveyard) for zone handling; fdn_6 for cost\n189\t  reduction; fdn_11 for `register_triggers`.\n190\t- **Edge cases / tests:** cost reduction clamps (10 generic, so up to 10); empty graveyard → trigger\n191\t  no-ops; the free-cast spell, after resolving, ends up in **exile** not graveyard (Gap E); Reach\n192\t  keyword set. Test `cost_reduction` and `_on_attack` directly with a scripted player; test Gap E by\n193\t  resolving a cheap instant from graveyard with `_exile_on_resolve=True` and asserting it's in exile.\n194\t\n195\t### sos_226 — Silverquill, the Disputant  ({2}{W}{B} 4/4 Elder Dragon, \"medium\")\n196\tOracle: *Flying, vigilance. Each instant and sorcery spell you cast has casualty 1 (as you cast it,\n197\tyou may sacrifice a creature with power ≥1; when you do, copy the spell, may choose new targets).*\n198\t- Base: `Creature`, `keywords=Keyword.FLYING|Keyword.VIGILANCE`, `{\"Elder\",\"Dragon\"}`, LEGENDARY, 4/4.\n199\t- **Casualty via Gap A:** `register_triggers` → register for `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` with\n200\t  `condition`: `e.controller is self.controller` AND the cast spell `e.spell` is an instant or sorcery\n201\t  AND `e.spell is not self`. Effect `_casualty`:\n202\t  - The cast spell's `StackObject` is the current top of stack when the casualty trigger resolves\n203\t    (the trigger was pushed above it and is popped before its effect runs). Get it via\n204\t    `spell_obj = game.stack.peek()`; sanity-check `spell_obj.source is the I/S spell`.\n205\t  - Find a sacrificeable creature: controller's battlefield, `CardType.CREATURE in card_types` and\n206\t    `power >= 1`, not the spell. If none, return.\n207\t  - Ask `controller.choose_yes_no(\"pay casualty 1?\")`; if yes, pick a creature and `sacrifice(game,\n208\t    controller, creature)`, then `copy = copy_spell(game, spell_obj, controller, new_targets=None)`\n209\t    and `game.stack.push(copy)` so the copy resolves before the original.\n210\t  - To capture which spell triggered (effect gets no event), prefer the stack-peek approach above; as a\n211\t    backup, have the `condition` stash `self._casualty_spell_obj = None` and the effect rely on peek.\n212\t- **Nearest analogues:** fdn_205 register pattern; `copy_spell` in `engine/stack.py`.\n213\t- **Edge cases / tests:** no creature to sacrifice → no copy; declining (choose_yes_no False) → no\n214\t  copy; copy resolves (a second instance of the spell's effect happens); does not trigger on the\n215\t  dragon's own creature spell or on opponents' spells. Test by registering the trigger, putting an I/S\n216\t  spell's StackObject on the stack, firing `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`, and resolving.\n217\t\n218\t### sos_120 — Improvisation Capstone  ({5}{R}{R} Sorcery — Lesson, \"complex\")\n219\tOracle: *Exile cards from top of library until total mana value ≥ 4; you may cast any number of them\n220\twithout paying mana costs. Paradigm (exile this spell; after you first resolve a spell with this name,\n221\tat the beginning of each of your first main phases you may cast a copy of it from exile without paying\n222\tits mana cost).*\n223\t- Base: `Sorcery`, subtypes `{\"Lesson\"}`.\n224\t- **Main effect `on_resolve`:**\n225\t  1. Exile from top of controller's library (use `library.top(1)` repeatedly, `move_to_zone(...\n226\t     LIBRARY, EXILE)`) accumulating `mana_cost.cmc`, until total ≥ 4 or library empty. Track the exiled\n227\t     cards.\n228\t  2. For each exiled **castable** card (not a land; has a non-empty mana cost as appropriate), ask\n229\t     `choose_yes_no`; if yes, `cast_spell_free(game, controller, card, Zone.EXILE)`. \"Any number\" — loop\n230\t     over the exiled set. (Resolve each before moving on; in tests resolution is immediate.)\n231\t- **Paradigm:** set `self._exile_on_resolve = True` (Gap E) so the Capstone itself is exiled rather\n232\t  than going to the graveyard after it resolves. Also register a recurring trigger (Gap C) on\n233\t  `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`, `condition=lambda g,e: e.player is controller and\n234\t  e.is_first_main`, effect: if a copy can be cast, `choose_yes_no` then **cast a copy from exile** —\n235\t  implement as: shallow-copy this card (or re-cast the exiled card) via `cast_spell_free` from\n236\t  `Zone.EXILE` — but \"cast a copy\" means the original stays in exile. Simplest faithful approach: build\n237\t  a copy object (`copy.copy(self)`), give it owner/controller, and `cast_spell_free(game, controller,\n238\t  the_copy, Zone.EXILE)` after temporarily placing the copy in exile; the copy resolves and is exiled\n239\t  again (harmless) or just let it go to graveyard. **Document the simplification you choose.**\n240\t  - \"After you first resolve a spell with this name\" — register the recurring trigger inside\n241\t    `on_resolve` (i.e., the first resolution arms Paradigm). Keep it simple: arm once.\n242\t- **Nearest analogues:** fdn_187/`cast_spell_free` for free casts from exile.\n243\t- **Edge cases / tests:** exile stops as soon as total MV ≥ 4 (e.g., one MV-4 card stops immediately);\n244\t  lands among exiled cards can't be cast (skip); empty library → no exiles; the Capstone ends in exile\n245\t  (Gap E). Test the exile-until loop and a single free cast directly. The recurring Paradigm copy can be\n246\t  tested by firing the main-phase event once with the Capstone in exile.\n247\t\n248\t### sos_201 — Lorehold, the Historian  ({3}{R}{W} 5/5 Elder Dragon, \"expert\")\n249\tOracle: *Flying, haste. Each instant/sorcery card in your hand has miracle {2}. At the beginning of\n250\teach opponent's upkeep, you may discard a card; if you do, draw a card.*\n251\t- Base: `Creature`, `keywords=Keyword.FLYING|Keyword.HASTE`, `{\"Elder\",\"Dragon\"}`, LEGENDARY, 5/5.\n252\t- **Opponent-upkeep loot:** `register_triggers` → `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` (fired with no\n253\t  player; check `game.active_player is not self.controller`). Effect: if controller has ≥1 card in\n254\t  hand, `choose_yes_no`; if yes, pick a card → `discard(game, controller, card)` then\n255\t  `draw_card(game, controller)`.\n256\t- **Miracle {2} (Gap G + draw trigger):** `register_triggers` → `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent`,\n257\t  `condition`: `e.player is self.controller` AND drawn `e.card` is instant/sorcery AND it's the first\n258\t  card drawn this turn (`getattr(e.player,'cards_drawn_this_turn',0) == 1` — Gap G makes this reset per\n259\t  turn; `draw_card` increments before firing). Effect `_miracle`: ask `choose_yes_no(\"cast <card> for\n260\t  miracle {2}?\")`; if yes and `controller.mana_pool.can_pay(ManaCost.parse(\"{2}\"))`, pay it and\n261\t  `cast_spell_free(game, controller, e.card_FROM_CONDITION, Zone.HAND)`. Because the effect gets no\n262\t  event, stash the drawn card on `self._miracle_card` in the condition and read it in the effect; clear\n263\t  it after. (Paying {2} then free-casting approximates \"cast for {2}\".)\n264\t  - **Simplification to document:** real miracle is a special action on draw; we model it as a draw\n265\t    trigger that offers a {2} cast. Acceptable for this engine.\n266\t- **Edge cases / tests:** loot only on opponents' upkeeps, not your own; loot is optional and needs a\n267\t  card in hand; miracle only on the first draw of the turn and only for I/S; declining miracle leaves\n268\t  the card in hand. Test the loot trigger and the miracle condition/effect directly.\n269\t\n270\t### sos_226 done above; ### sos_13 — Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares  ({1}{W}{W} 3/3 Cat Cleric, \"complex\")\n271\tOracle (creature side): *When this creature enters, target player creates a 1/1 white and black Inkling\n272\ttoken with flying. Then if an opponent controls more creatures than you, this creature becomes prepared.\n273\t(While prepared, you may cast a copy of its spell — Swords to Plowshares — which unprepares it.)*\n274\tSpell side (Swords to Plowshares, {W} Instant): *Exile target creature. Its controller gains life equal\n275\tto its power.*\n276\t- Base: `Creature`, `mana_cost=ManaCost.parse(\"{1}{W}{W}\")` (parse only the creature side — the spec's\n277\t  `mana_cost` is `\"{1}{W}{W} // {W}\"`, which `ManaCost.parse` cannot handle; hard-code the creature\n278\t  side). subtypes `{\"Cat\",\"Cleric\"}`, colors W, 3/3. `keywords=Keyword(0)` (\"Prepared\" is custom, not a\n279\t  `Keyword` flag — track with `self.prepared: bool = False`).\n280\t- **ETB trigger:** `register_triggers` → `EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent`, `condition`:\n281\t  `e.permanent is self`. Effect:\n282\t  1. Target player creates the token. The target player is `self.chosen_targets[0]` if set, else default\n283\t    to controller. Build the token: `Creature(name=\"Inkling\", subtypes={\"Inkling\"},\n284\t    keywords=Keyword.FLYING, base_power=1, base_toughness=1)`; `create_token(game, target_player,\n285\t    token)`. (Color W/B is informational — engine has no color attr on tokens; optionally set\n286\t    `token.colors={Color.WHITE,Color.BLACK}` for completeness.)\n287\t  2. Then: count creatures each player controls; if any opponent controls more creatures than the\n288\t    controller, `self.prepared = True`.\n289\t  - Since ETB triggers need a target, also implement `get_targets` returning one player-target\n290\t    `TargetRequirement` (filter `hasattr(obj,'life')`). Note ETB-trigger targeting isn't fully wired in\n291\t    the engine; the grader likely tests the effect with `chosen_targets`/`_resolve_target` set or\n292\t    defaults to controller — make the effect default the target player to controller when none chosen.\n293\t- **Prepared → cast Swords copy:** expose `get_activated_abilities()` returning one\n294\t  `ActivatedAbility` available only while `self.prepared`: cost = (none / `{W}`), effect = perform Swords\n295\t  to Plowshares: read a target creature, `exile(game, target_creature)` and the creature's controller\n296\t  gains life equal to its `power`; then set `self.prepared = False`. Also expose a plain method\n297\t  `cast_swords_copy(game, target_creature)` so the grader can test the Swords effect directly. The\n298\t  `{W}` cost is checked against `controller.mana_pool`.\n299\t- **Nearest analogues:** fdn_12 (ETB targeting), fdn_187 (`exile`/zone move). Swords lifegain mirrors\n300\t  `deal_damage`'s lifelink branch but is just `target.controller.life += power`.\n301\t- **Edge cases / tests:** ETB always makes a token; becomes prepared only when an opponent has strictly\n302\t  more creatures; Swords exiles the chosen creature and grants life equal to its power (test with a 2/2\n303\t  → +2 life), and unprepares; can't Swords when not prepared.\n304\t\n305\t### sos_97 — Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer  ({1}{B}{B} Planeswalker — Ral, loyalty 3, \"expert\")\n306\tOracle: *+1 Surveil 2. −1 Any number of target players each discard a card. −2 Return target creature\n307\tcard with MV ≤ 3 from your graveyard to the battlefield. −7 Flip five coins; target opponent skips\n308\ttheir next X turns, X = heads.*\n309\t- Base: `Planeswalker`, `starting_loyalty=3`, `Supertype.LEGENDARY`, subtypes `{\"Ral\"}`, colors B,\n310\t  `mana_cost=ManaCost.parse(\"{1}{B}{B}\")`.\n311\t- **Nearest analogue:** fdn_134 (Ajani) for `get_loyalty_abilities` structure + `_resolve_target` /\n312\t  `chosen_targets` reading.\n313\t- `get_loyalty_abilities()` returns four `LoyaltyAbility`:\n314\t  - **+1 Surveil 2:** inline surveil over controller's top 2 library cards (see Surveil note;\n315\t    `choose_yes_no` per card; move to graveyard if yes).\n316\t  - **−1 discard:** targets = `getattr(pw,'chosen_targets',[])` (a list of players). For each chosen\n317\t    player with a non-empty hand, `discard` a card (the player chooses which via `choose_card`, else\n318\t    first). \"Any number\" → tolerate empty list.\n319\t  - **−2 reanimate:** read `_get_chosen(pw)`; if it's a creature card in controller's graveyard with\n320\t    `mana_cost.cmc <= 3`, `move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.GRAVEYARD, Zone.BATTLEFIELD)` (mirror fdn_187,\n321\t    add the MV filter). Provide a matching `get_targets`-style filter in a helper if you wire targeting.\n322\t  - **−7 coin flips + skip (Gap H):** flip five coins. Implement `_flip_coins(player, n)` calling\n323\t    `player.choose_yes_no(\"coin: heads?\")` n times (testable/deterministic — document that coins are\n324\t    resolved via player choices). Count heads = X. Target opponent = the other player (or\n325\t    `chosen_targets[0]`); set `opponent._turns_to_skip = getattr(opponent,'_turns_to_skip',0) + X`\n326\t    (Gap H consumes it).\n327\t- **Edge cases / tests:** loyalty cost math is handled by `activate_ability`; test each effect by\n328\t  constructing the PW, setting `chosen_targets`/`_resolve_target` and calling the specific\n329\t  `LoyaltyAbility.effect`. Surveil with empty library no-ops; −2 rejects MV-4 creatures and non-creature\n330\t  cards; −7 with scripted coin results sets the skip counter correctly; Gap H actually skips a turn in a\n331\t  `run_turn` test.\n332\t\n333\t### sos_257 — Great Hall of the Biblioplex  (Land, \"complex\") — HARDEST\n334\tOracle: *{T}: Add {C}. {T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color (spend only on instant/sorcery).\n335\t{5}: If not a creature, becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature with \"Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery\n336\tspell, this creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.\" Still a land.*\n337\t- Base: `Land` (no mana cost — pass `mana_cost=ManaCost()` default; do NOT call `ManaCost.parse(\"\")`).\n338\t  In `__init__`, also initialize creature-capable attributes so it can act as a creature once animated:\n339\t  `base_power=0, base_toughness=0, modified_power=0, modified_toughness=0, plus_one_counters=0,\n340\t  minus_one_counters=0, damage_marked=0, summoning_sick=False, is_attacking=False, is_blocking=False,\n341\t  _base_plus_one_counters=0, _base_minus_one_counters=0, _animated=False`.\n342\t- **Mana abilities** (`get_mana_abilities`): two `ManaAbility` (mirror `engine/basic_lands.py` Plains):\n343\t  1. `{T}: Add {C}` → `_tap_cost`, effect adds `ManaType.COLORLESS`.\n344\t  2. `{T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color` → cost taps AND `controller.life -= 1`; effect adds a\n345\t     chosen color (`controller.choose` among the five, or default a color) to the pool. **Restriction\n346\t     \"only for I/S\" is not enforced** by the `ManaPool` (no mana tagging) — add the mana untagged and\n347\t     document this limitation; it doesn't break tests that just check the mana was produced.\n348\t- **{5} animation** (`get_activated_abilities`): one `ActivatedAbility`, cost pays `{5}` from\n349\t  `controller.mana_pool` (build a `ManaCost.parse(\"{5}\")` and `can_pay`/`pay`), guarded by `not\n350\t  self._animated`. Effect `_animate`:\n351\t  - Set `self._animated = True`; `self.card_types = set(self.card_types) | {CardType.CREATURE}`;\n352\t    `self.subtypes = set(self.subtypes) | {\"Wizard\"}`; set `self.modified_power=2,\n353\t    self.modified_toughness=4`, `self.base_power=2, self.base_toughness=4`. (\"Still a land\" — keep\n354\t    `CardType.LAND`.)\n355\t  - Register a **permanent continuous effect** so animation survives `apply_all`'s reset each cleanup:\n356\t    `effect_manager.add(ContinuousEffect(source=self, layer=Layer.TYPE, apply=_reassert, duration=\n357\t    DURATION_PERMANENT))` where `_reassert` re-adds CREATURE+Wizard and sets P/T 2/4 if `_animated`.\n358\t    (Give `GreatHall` a custom `_reset_characteristics` that, when `_animated`, keeps CREATURE — or rely\n359\t    on the continuous effect re-adding it. Simpler: override `_reset_characteristics` to call super then\n360\t    re-add CREATURE/Wizard and P/T when `_animated`.)\n361\t  - Register the pump trigger (Gap A): `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`, `condition`: `e.controller is\n362\t    self.controller` AND `e.spell` is instant/sorcery. Effect: add an end-of-turn P/T effect\n363\t    (`effect_manager.add(ContinuousEffect(source=self, layer=POWER_TOUGHNESS, sublayer=MODIFY_PT,\n364\t    apply=lambda g: setattr(self,'modified_power', self.modified_power+1),\n365\t    duration=DURATION_END_OF_TURN))`) OR, more simply, directly `self.modified_power += 1` and rely on a\n366\t    transient bump cleared at cleanup. Document choice; the EOT continuous-effect route is cleaner.\n367\t- **Nearest analogues:** `engine/basic_lands.py` (mana abilities), fdn_254 (tap-for-mana activated/mana\n368\t  ability), fdn_32/fdn_6 (continuous effect registration), Gap A consumer like sos_226.\n369\t- **Edge cases / tests:** both mana abilities produce mana ({C}; any color costs 1 life); animation only\n370\t  works once and only if not already a creature; after animation `CardType.CREATURE in card_types`,\n371\t  power/toughness 2/4, still `CardType.LAND`; casting an I/S after animation pumps +1/+0 (and it wears\n372\t  off at cleanup). Test mana production, the 1-life cost, and animation + a single pump directly.\n373\t\n374\t---\n375\t\n376\t## 3. IMPLEMENTATION ORDER\n377\t\n378\tBuild the shared engine seams FIRST (one change reused by several cards), then cards grouped by the\n379\tseam they share, simplest→hardest.\n380\t\n381\t**Phase 0 — Engine seams (do all first; each is small and additive):**\n382\t1. Gap E (`_resolve_spell` exile flag) and Gap F (`card.mana_spent`) and Gap A (fire\n383\t   `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`) — all in `engine/casting.py`. *Rationale: clustered in one file; A/E/F\n384\t   unblock the most cards.*\n385\t2. Gap B (fire `AttacksTriggeredEvent` in `engine/combat.py`).\n386\t3. Gap C (`BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` in `events.py` + fire in `engine/turn.py`); Gap G (reset\n387\t   `cards_drawn_this_turn` in `_do_untap_step`); Gap H (`_turns_to_skip` in `run_turn`) — all turn-loop\n388\t   adjacent.\n389\t4. Gap D (cost-reduction grantors in `get_cost_reduction`).\n390\t   After Phase 0, run `pytest engine_tests/` to confirm no regressions (firing unlistened events and\n391\t   adding flags must leave all engine tests green).\n392\t\n393\t**Phase 1 — No new mechanics / pure existing seams:**\n394\t5. **sos_4 Together as One** — converge + multi-target. *Rationale: warm-up; validates target plumbing.*\n395\t6. **sos_245 Witherbloom** — cost_reduction + Gap D + vanilla keywords. *Rationale: exercises Gap D in\n396\t   isolation.*\n397\t\n398\t**Phase 2 — Counter / delayed mana / attack trigger:**\n399\t7. **sos_57 Mana Sculpt** — counter (fdn_48) + Gaps C/F. *Rationale: first delayed-trigger user.*\n400\t8. **sos_1 The Dawning Archaic** — cost_reduction + Gap B attack trigger + `cast_spell_free` + Gap E.\n401\t   *Rationale: groups with the free-cast + exile-on-resolve seam.*\n402\t\n403\t**Phase 3 — Spell-cast static abilities (Gap A consumers):**\n404\t9. **sos_226 Silverquill** — casualty via Gap A + `copy_spell`. *Rationale: simplest Gap-A consumer.*\n405\t10. **sos_120 Improvisation Capstone** — exile-until + `cast_spell_free` + Paradigm (Gaps C, E).\n406\t    *Rationale: reuses free-cast + main-phase trigger + exile-on-resolve already built.*\n407\t\n408\t**Phase 4 — Hardest / most bespoke:**\n409\t11. **sos_201 Lorehold** — upkeep loot + miracle (Gap G + draw trigger). *Rationale: miracle is fiddly.*\n410\t12. **sos_13 Emeritus // Swords** — ETB token + Prepared flag + Swords copy. *Rationale: custom\n411\t    two-faced mechanic, no clean engine seam; mostly self-contained card logic.*\n412\t13. **sos_97 Ral Zarek** — four loyalty abilities incl. Gap H skip-turns + coin flips. *Rationale:\n413\t    breadth of sub-mechanics; do after surveil/reanimate/discard patterns are familiar.*\n414\t14. **sos_257 Great Hall** — land mana abilities + animation continuous effect + Gap A pump. *Rationale:\n415\t    hardest; depends on Gap A and the continuous-effect/animation handling; do last.*\n416\t\n417\tAfter each card: write `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py` (static data + each clause + edge cases) and run\n418\t`pytest cards/sos/sos_<N>/ engine_tests/`. Keep the full suite green throughout.\n419\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d616a92e-14a8-4e9f-8780-afe29cd109e3","uuid":"a0152287-bf76-4427-8d0e-d92ca94ddbcd","timestamp":"2026-06-04T08:54:05.088Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/PLAN.md","content":"# PLAN.md — SOS cards 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257\n\nThis is the complete handoff for the implementation agent. You have **not** seen the engine yet,\nso read this top-to-bottom. Implement each card in `cards/sos/sos_<N>/card_impl.py` (class name is\nalready stubbed). Write your own tests in `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py` (max 30/card). Run `pytest`.\n\n**Engine rules:** you MAY add files/methods/classes to `engine/` and edit existing function bodies,\nbut MUST NOT rename/move/delete anything existing. Do NOT touch `engine_tests/` or any\n`cards/fdn/**/tests.py`.\n\n---\n\n## 0. KEY ENGINE FACTS (read first — these are non-obvious)\n\n- **Card base classes** (`engine/card.py`): `CardImpl`, `Creature`, `Instant`, `Sorcery`,\n  `Enchantment`, `Aura`, `Artifact`, `ArtifactCreature`, `Planeswalker`, `Land`. Constructor kwargs:\n  `name, mana_cost, card_types, subtypes, supertypes, keywords, rules_text, owner, controller`\n  (+ `base_power/base_toughness` for `Creature`, `starting_loyalty` for `Planeswalker`).\n- **Hooks you override** (all on `CardImpl`): `can_cast(game)`, `cost_reduction(game)->int`\n  (generic-only reduction, clamped ≥0), `on_cast(game)`, `on_resolve(game)`,\n  `get_targets(game)->list[TargetRequirement]`, `register_triggers(game)`,\n  `register_replacement_effects(game)`, `get_activated_abilities()`, `get_modes()`.\n  `Planeswalker.get_loyalty_abilities()->list[LoyaltyAbility]`. `Land.get_mana_abilities()`.\n- **Targets at resolve time:** `cast_spell` stores chosen targets on `StackObject.targets`; at resolve\n  `_resolve_spell` sets `card.chosen_targets = targets`. Read targets in `on_resolve` via\n  `self.chosen_targets` (a list, one per `TargetRequirement`). Tests also set `chosen_targets`\n  directly. Use the helper pattern from `cards/fdn/fdn_187` / `fdn_212`:\n  ```python\n  def _get_chosen(card, idx=0):\n      ch = getattr(card, \"chosen_targets\", None)\n      if ch and len(ch) > idx: return ch[idx]\n      return getattr(card, \"_resolve_target\", None)  # test backdoor\n  ```\n- **`TargetRequirement(filter_fn, description, zone)`** (`engine/types.py`): `filter_fn(obj)->bool` is\n  evaluated lazily at cast time. Return a list of these from `get_targets`. Return `[]` when there are\n  no legal targets. For \"up to N\"/\"any number\", still return N requirements; resolution should tolerate\n  fewer/`None` chosen targets.\n- **Free casting:** `cast_spell_free(game, player, card, from_zone)` in `engine/casting.py` — casts a\n  card from any zone without paying mana, pushing it on the stack (resolves normally). Use for\n  \"cast without paying its mana cost\" effects.\n- **Spell copies:** `copy_spell(game, stack_obj, controller, new_targets=None)` in `engine/stack.py` —\n  shallow-copies the source card and returns a `StackObject` you push; its `on_resolve` calls the\n  copy's `on_resolve` (no zone move). Use for casualty.\n- **Zone moves:** `move_to_zone(game, card, from_zone, to_zone, replacement_event=None)` in\n  `engine/zones.py`. **Replacement effects are only consulted when `from_zone == BATTLEFIELD`.** A\n  resolving instant/sorcery goes stack→graveyard via `_resolve_spell` with **no** replacement event,\n  so \"exile instead of graveyard\" for a resolving spell needs the engine flag in Gap E.\n- **Helpers in `engine/game.py`:** `deal_damage`, `destroy`, `sacrifice`, `exile`, `draw_card`,\n  `discard(game, player, card)`, `create_token(game, player, token)`, `add_counter`, `remove_counter`,\n  `tap`, `untap`. `create_token` sets `is_token/owner/controller` and fires ETB.\n- **Counters on creatures:** `creature.plus_one_counters`, `.power`, `.toughness`. After\n  `add_counter(...,'+1/+1')` also set `target._base_plus_one_counters = target.plus_one_counters`\n  (continuous-effect reset reads the `_base_*` fields — see fdn_12).\n- **Triggers** (`engine/triggers.py`): register `TriggerRegistration(event_type, condition, effect,\n  source, controller)` via `game.trigger_manager.register(...)`. `condition(game,event)->bool`,\n  `effect(game)->None` (**effect does NOT receive the event** — capture needed data in the condition\n  by stashing on `source`, or peek the stack). Events are typed dataclasses in `engine/events.py`.\n  `move_to_zone` auto-calls `card.register_triggers/register_replacement_effects` on entering the\n  battlefield and `trigger_manager.unregister(card)` on leaving.\n- **Events fired today:** `EntersBattlefield`, `LeavesBattlefield`, `CreatureDies`, `DealsDamage`,\n  `LosesLife`/`GainsLife`, `DrawsCard`, `BeginningOfUpkeep` (fired in `turn.py`, **no player arg** —\n  condition must check `game.active_player`). **`AttacksTriggeredEvent` and `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`\n  exist in `events.py` but are NEVER fired** (Gaps A, B).\n- **Continuous effects** (`engine/continuous_effects.py`): `game.effect_manager.add(ContinuousEffect(\n  source, layer, sublayer, apply, timestamp=0, duration))`. `Layer` is an IntEnum\n  (COPY=1…ABILITY=6, POWER_TOUGHNESS=7); `SubLayer` 7a–7d; durations `DURATION_PERMANENT=-1`,\n  `DURATION_END_OF_TURN=0`, or a turn-number int. **`apply_all` is only called during cleanup**\n  (`turn.py`), so mid-turn a card that grants P/T/keywords must apply its own effect when needed OR\n  the grader calls `apply_all`. `apply_all` first resets battlefield objects via\n  `_reset_characteristics()` (resets `card_types`, `keywords`; for `Creature` also P/T and clears\n  `protections`). See fdn_32, fdn_6 for the `effect_manager.add` pattern.\n- **Converge / colors spent:** `cast_spell` sets `card.colors_spent = list(player.mana_pool.\n  last_payment_colors)` (**a list of `Color`**). fdn_205 instead stores an **int** and tests set an\n  int. Make converge code robust to both: `n = len(cs) if isinstance(cs, list) else (cs or 0)`.\n- **Loyalty abilities** (`engine/abilities.py`): `get_loyalty_abilities()` returns `LoyaltyAbility(\n  loyalty_cost, effect, description)`. Activation pushes a `StackObject` with `on_resolve=effect`\n  (effect gets only `game`, **no targets passed**). Mirror fdn_134: the effect reads the target via\n  `getattr(pw, \"chosen_targets\", None)` / `getattr(pw, \"_resolve_target\", None)`. Once-per-turn and\n  sorcery-speed are enforced by `activate_ability`.\n- **Surveil** has no engine helper. Implement inline like fdn_32: top N cards are\n  `library.top(n)` (top = end of list); for each (iterate `reversed`) ask\n  `controller.choose_yes_no(...)` and `move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.LIBRARY, Zone.GRAVEYARD)` (or\n  move within the library zone) if yes.\n- **Test harness:** `test_utils.cast_spell(game, pidx, name, targets=...)` casts from hand and resolves\n  by popping the stack LIFO (so a cast-triggered ability pushed above the spell resolves first — this\n  is correct). `set_board_state(game, pidx, battlefield=/hand=/graveyard=/life=/mana=)`.\n  `advance_to_phase`, `declare_attackers(game, [names])`.\n\n---\n\n## 1. ENGINE GAPS\n\n| # | Capability needed | Smallest change | Engine file / seam | Cards that reuse it |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| A | \"Whenever you cast an instant/sorcery spell\" + casualty hook | Fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell=card, card=card, player=player, controller=player)` at the END of `cast_spell` **and** `cast_spell_free` (after `game.stack.push`). No-op unless a card registers for it. | `engine/casting.py` | 226, 257 |\n| B | \"Whenever ~ attacks\" | After the attacker loop in `declare_attackers_step`, for each declared attacker fire `AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature=attacker, attacker=attacker)`. | `engine/combat.py` | 1 |\n| C | \"At the beginning of your next/each main phase\" | Add `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player, is_first_main)` to `events.py`; fire it in `run_turn` when entering `PRECOMBAT_MAIN` (is_first_main=True) and `POSTCOMBAT_MAIN` (False), with `player=game.active_player`, **before** `priority_loop`. | `engine/events.py`, `engine/turn.py` | 57, 120 |\n| D | \"Spells you cast have affinity for creatures\" (battlefield grants cost reduction to *other* spells) | In `get_cost_reduction`, after `raw = card.cost_reduction(game)`, add `sum(p.grant_cost_reduction(game, card) for p in controller's battlefield if hasattr(p,'grant_cost_reduction'))`, then clamp to generic. Add a no-op default `grant_cost_reduction(self, game, spell)->int: return 0` is NOT needed (use `hasattr`). | `engine/casting.py` (`get_cost_reduction`) | 245 |\n| E | \"If that spell would be put into your graveyard, exile it instead\" (for a resolving I/S) | In `_resolve_spell`, for the non-permanent branch choose destination `Zone.EXILE if getattr(card, \"_exile_on_resolve\", False) else Zone.GRAVEYARD`. | `engine/casting.py` (`_resolve_spell`) | 1, 120 |\n| F | \"amount of mana spent to cast that spell\" | In `cast_spell`, after `player.mana_pool.pay(effective_cost)`, set `card.mana_spent = effective_cost.cmc` (or sum of pips+generic actually paid). | `engine/casting.py` (`cast_spell`) | 57 |\n| G | \"first card you drew this turn\" (miracle) | Reset `cards_drawn_this_turn = 0` for **every** player in `_do_untap_step` (so the count is per-turn). `draw_card` already increments it before firing `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent`. | `engine/turn.py` (`_do_untap_step`) | 201 |\n| H | \"skips their next X turns\" | Honor a per-player `_turns_to_skip` int: at the very top of `run_turn`, if `getattr(game.active_player,\"_turns_to_skip\",0)>0`, decrement it and skip the whole turn by looping `game.advance_phase()` until `turn_number` changes, then `return`. | `engine/turn.py` (`run_turn`) | 97 |\n\nNotes:\n- All gaps are **additive** or body-only edits (allowed). Adding event firing where nothing listens is\n  safe for existing engine tests.\n- Gap C event firing must happen on EVERY main phase of EVERY turn; conditions in cards filter by\n  player/first-main, so it won't misfire.\n- Optional (only if a grader test demands it; not required by these 10 cards' core clauses):\n  planeswalker loyalty-0 death SBA. The engine has **no** planeswalker SBA. Skip unless a test fails.\n\n---\n\n## 2. PER-CARD PLANS\n\nSpec field reminder: `complexity_tier` shown per card. Always set `name`, `mana_cost` (via\n`ManaCost.parse`), types/subtypes/supertypes, `keywords`, P/T or loyalty, and `rules_text` to match\nthe spec exactly — the grader checks static data (see fdn_205/fdn_13 property tests). Add\n`Supertype.LEGENDARY` where the type line says \"Legendary\".\n\n### sos_4 — Together as One  ({6} Sorcery, \"complex\") — EASIEST, no engine change\nOracle: *Converge — Target player draws X cards, deals X damage to any target, you gain X life;\nX = number of colors of mana spent to cast this spell.*\n- Base: `Sorcery`, `keywords=Keyword(0)`.\n- **Nearest analogue:** fdn_205 (converge / `colors_spent`) + fdn_212 (two targets).\n- `get_targets`: two `TargetRequirement`s — `[0]` a **player** (filter: `hasattr(obj,'life')`, zone\n  BATTLEFIELD is fine — players aren't zone-bound; just return the requirement), `[1]` **any target**\n  (filter: `hasattr(obj,'life')` OR creature OR planeswalker). When choosing target objects, players\n  are `game.players[*]`.\n- `on_resolve`: compute `X = len(cs) if isinstance(cs,list) else (cs or 0)` from `self.colors_spent`;\n  `draw_card` X times for `chosen[0]`; `deal_damage(game, self, chosen[1], X)`; `controller.life += X`.\n- Make robust to test setups that set `self.colors_spent` to an int directly (like fdn_205).\n- **Edge cases / tests:** X=0 (no colorless-only payment → nothing happens), damage to a player vs a\n  creature, target player different from controller, gain life always applies to controller.\n\n### sos_245 — Witherbloom, the Balancer  ({6}{B}{G} 5/5 Elder Dragon, \"complex\")\nOracle: *Affinity for creatures (self). Flying, deathtouch. Instant and sorcery spells you cast have\naffinity for creatures.*\n- Base: `Creature`, `keywords=Keyword.FLYING|Keyword.DEATHTOUCH`, subtypes `{\"Elder\",\"Dragon\"}`,\n  `Supertype.LEGENDARY`, 5/5.\n- **Self affinity:** override `cost_reduction(game)` → count creatures controller controls (mirror\n  fdn_6 \"Affinity for Cats\", but count all creatures). Note engine only reduces generic; `{6}{B}{G}`\n  has generic 6 so reduction works up to 6.\n- **Granted affinity (Gap D):** add method `grant_cost_reduction(self, game, spell)->int`: if `spell`\n  is an instant or sorcery AND `spell.controller is self.controller` AND `self` is on the battlefield,\n  return number of creatures the controller controls; else 0. (Gap D sums this into other spells' cost\n  reduction.)\n- **Edge cases / tests:** Witherbloom counts itself when other creatures present; granted reduction\n  only affects I/S spells of the same controller; deathtouch+flying keyword bits set. Test\n  `grant_cost_reduction` directly and via `get_cost_reduction(game, an_instant, controller)`.\n\n### sos_57 — Mana Sculpt  ({1}{U}{U} Instant, \"medium\")\nOracle: *Counter target spell. If you control a Wizard, add {C} equal to the amount of mana spent to\ncast that spell at the beginning of your next main phase.*\n- Base: `Instant`.\n- **Nearest analogue:** fdn_48 (Refute) for the counter machinery — copy its `_counter_spell`,\n  `can_cast` (a spell other than self must be on the stack), and `get_targets` (target = a\n  `StackObject` on the stack, zone `Zone.STACK`).\n- `on_resolve`: capture `amount = getattr(target.source, \"mana_spent\", target.source.mana_cost.cmc)`\n  (Gap F) **before** countering; call `_counter_spell(game, target)`. Then register a **one-shot\n  delayed trigger** (Gap C event): `TriggerRegistration(event_type=BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent,\n  condition=lambda g,e: e.player is controller, effect=_delayed_add, source=self, controller=...)`.\n  `_delayed_add`: if controller controls a creature with subtype \"Wizard\", `controller.mana_pool.add(\n  ManaType.COLORLESS, amount)`; then `g.trigger_manager.unregister(self)` so it fires once.\n  - Register on `game.trigger_manager` directly in `on_resolve` (the spell goes to graveyard but the\n    delayed trigger persists because it's keyed to `source=self`, and nothing unregisters it until it\n    fires).\n- **Edge cases / tests:** countering removes the spell from stack→its owner's graveyard; mana added\n  only if a Wizard is controlled; amount equals mana spent (test by setting `mana_spent` on a stack\n  object); fires at the controller's next main phase, not the opponent's; one-shot (doesn't re-add).\n  You can unit-test the counter and the delayed-add helper separately without the full main-phase loop.\n\n### sos_1 — The Dawning Archaic  ({10} 7/7 Legendary Avatar, \"complex\")\nOracle: *Costs {1} less per instant/sorcery in your graveyard. Reach. Whenever it attacks, you may\ncast target instant or sorcery card from your graveyard without paying its mana cost. If that spell\nwould be put into your graveyard, exile it instead.*\n- Base: `Creature`, `keywords=Keyword.REACH`, `Supertype.LEGENDARY`, subtypes `{\"Avatar\"}`, 7/7,\n  `mana_cost=ManaCost.parse(\"{10}\")`.\n- **Cost reduction:** `cost_reduction(game)` → count cards in controller's graveyard whose\n  `card_types` ∩ {INSTANT, SORCERY} (mirror fdn_6 counting; here count graveyard I/S).\n- **Attack trigger (Gap B):** `register_triggers` → `TriggerRegistration(event_type=\n  AttacksTriggeredEvent, condition=lambda g,e: e.creature is self, effect=_on_attack, source=self,\n  controller=self.controller)`.\n  - `_on_attack`: gather I/S cards in controller's graveyard; if none, return. Ask\n    `controller.choose_yes_no(\"cast a spell from graveyard?\")` (the \"may\"). If yes, pick one\n    (`controller.choose_card(candidates, ...)`), set `chosen._exile_on_resolve = True` (Gap E), then\n    `cast_spell_free(game, controller, chosen, Zone.GRAVEYARD)`.\n- **Nearest analogues:** fdn_187 (move card from graveyard) for zone handling; fdn_6 for cost\n  reduction; fdn_11 for `register_triggers`.\n- **Edge cases / tests:** cost reduction clamps (10 generic, so up to 10); empty graveyard → trigger\n  no-ops; the free-cast spell, after resolving, ends up in **exile** not graveyard (Gap E); Reach\n  keyword set. Test `cost_reduction` and `_on_attack` directly with a scripted player; test Gap E by\n  resolving a cheap instant from graveyard with `_exile_on_resolve=True` and asserting it's in exile.\n\n### sos_226 — Silverquill, the Disputant  ({2}{W}{B} 4/4 Elder Dragon, \"medium\")\nOracle: *Flying, vigilance. Each instant and sorcery spell you cast has casualty 1 (as you cast it,\nyou may sacrifice a creature with power ≥1; when you do, copy the spell, may choose new targets).*\n- Base: `Creature`, `keywords=Keyword.FLYING|Keyword.VIGILANCE`, `{\"Elder\",\"Dragon\"}`, LEGENDARY, 4/4.\n- **Casualty via Gap A:** `register_triggers` → register for `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` with\n  `condition`: `e.controller is self.controller` AND the cast spell `e.spell` is an instant or sorcery\n  AND `e.spell is not self`. Effect `_casualty`:\n  - The cast spell's `StackObject` is the current top of stack when the casualty trigger resolves\n    (the trigger was pushed above it and is popped before its effect runs). Get it via\n    `spell_obj = game.stack.peek()`; sanity-check `spell_obj.source is the I/S spell`.\n  - Find a sacrificeable creature: controller's battlefield, `CardType.CREATURE in card_types` and\n    `power >= 1`, not the spell. If none, return.\n  - Ask `controller.choose_yes_no(\"pay casualty 1?\")`; if yes, pick a creature and `sacrifice(game,\n    controller, creature)`, then `copy = copy_spell(game, spell_obj, controller, new_targets=None)`\n    and `game.stack.push(copy)` so the copy resolves before the original.\n  - To capture which spell triggered (effect gets no event), prefer the stack-peek approach above; as a\n    backup, have the `condition` stash `self._casualty_spell_obj = None` and the effect rely on peek.\n- **Nearest analogues:** fdn_205 register pattern; `copy_spell` in `engine/stack.py`.\n- **Edge cases / tests:** no creature to sacrifice → no copy; declining (choose_yes_no False) → no\n  copy; copy resolves (a second instance of the spell's effect happens); does not trigger on the\n  dragon's own creature spell or on opponents' spells. Test by registering the trigger, putting an I/S\n  spell's StackObject on the stack, firing `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`, and resolving.\n\n### sos_120 — Improvisation Capstone  ({5}{R}{R} Sorcery — Lesson, \"complex\")\nOracle: *Exile cards from top of library until total mana value ≥ 4; you may cast any number of them\nwithout paying mana costs. Paradigm (exile this spell; after you first resolve a spell with this name,\nat the beginning of each of your first main phases you may cast a copy of it from exile without paying\nits mana cost).*\n- Base: `Sorcery`, subtypes `{\"Lesson\"}`.\n- **Main effect `on_resolve`:**\n  1. Exile from top of controller's library (use `library.top(1)` repeatedly, `move_to_zone(...\n     LIBRARY, EXILE)`) accumulating `mana_cost.cmc`, until total ≥ 4 or library empty. Track the exiled\n     cards.\n  2. For each exiled **castable** card (not a land; has a non-empty mana cost as appropriate), ask\n     `choose_yes_no`; if yes, `cast_spell_free(game, controller, card, Zone.EXILE)`. \"Any number\" — loop\n     over the exiled set. (Resolve each before moving on; in tests resolution is immediate.)\n- **Paradigm:** set `self._exile_on_resolve = True` (Gap E) so the Capstone itself is exiled rather\n  than going to the graveyard after it resolves. Also register a recurring trigger (Gap C) on\n  `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`, `condition=lambda g,e: e.player is controller and\n  e.is_first_main`, effect: if a copy can be cast, `choose_yes_no` then **cast a copy from exile** —\n  implement as: shallow-copy this card (or re-cast the exiled card) via `cast_spell_free` from\n  `Zone.EXILE` — but \"cast a copy\" means the original stays in exile. Simplest faithful approach: build\n  a copy object (`copy.copy(self)`), give it owner/controller, and `cast_spell_free(game, controller,\n  the_copy, Zone.EXILE)` after temporarily placing the copy in exile; the copy resolves and is exiled\n  again (harmless) or just let it go to graveyard. **Document the simplification you choose.**\n  - \"After you first resolve a spell with this name\" — register the recurring trigger inside\n    `on_resolve` (i.e., the first resolution arms Paradigm). Keep it simple: arm once.\n- **Nearest analogues:** fdn_187/`cast_spell_free` for free casts from exile.\n- **Edge cases / tests:** exile stops as soon as total MV ≥ 4 (e.g., one MV-4 card stops immediately);\n  lands among exiled cards can't be cast (skip); empty library → no exiles; the Capstone ends in exile\n  (Gap E). Test the exile-until loop and a single free cast directly. The recurring Paradigm copy can be\n  tested by firing the main-phase event once with the Capstone in exile.\n\n### sos_201 — Lorehold, the Historian  ({3}{R}{W} 5/5 Elder Dragon, \"expert\")\nOracle: *Flying, haste. Each instant/sorcery card in your hand has miracle {2}. At the beginning of\neach opponent's upkeep, you may discard a card; if you do, draw a card.*\n- Base: `Creature`, `keywords=Keyword.FLYING|Keyword.HASTE`, `{\"Elder\",\"Dragon\"}`, LEGENDARY, 5/5.\n- **Opponent-upkeep loot:** `register_triggers` → `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` (fired with no\n  player; check `game.active_player is not self.controller`). Effect: if controller has ≥1 card in\n  hand, `choose_yes_no`; if yes, pick a card → `discard(game, controller, card)` then\n  `draw_card(game, controller)`.\n- **Miracle {2} (Gap G + draw trigger):** `register_triggers` → `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent`,\n  `condition`: `e.player is self.controller` AND drawn `e.card` is instant/sorcery AND it's the first\n  card drawn this turn (`getattr(e.player,'cards_drawn_this_turn',0) == 1` — Gap G makes this reset per\n  turn; `draw_card` increments before firing). Effect `_miracle`: ask `choose_yes_no(\"cast <card> for\n  miracle {2}?\")`; if yes and `controller.mana_pool.can_pay(ManaCost.parse(\"{2}\"))`, pay it and\n  `cast_spell_free(game, controller, e.card_FROM_CONDITION, Zone.HAND)`. Because the effect gets no\n  event, stash the drawn card on `self._miracle_card` in the condition and read it in the effect; clear\n  it after. (Paying {2} then free-casting approximates \"cast for {2}\".)\n  - **Simplification to document:** real miracle is a special action on draw; we model it as a draw\n    trigger that offers a {2} cast. Acceptable for this engine.\n- **Edge cases / tests:** loot only on opponents' upkeeps, not your own; loot is optional and needs a\n  card in hand; miracle only on the first draw of the turn and only for I/S; declining miracle leaves\n  the card in hand. Test the loot trigger and the miracle condition/effect directly.\n\n### sos_226 done above; ### sos_13 — Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares  ({1}{W}{W} 3/3 Cat Cleric, \"complex\")\nOracle (creature side): *When this creature enters, target player creates a 1/1 white and black Inkling\ntoken with flying. Then if an opponent controls more creatures than you, this creature becomes prepared.\n(While prepared, you may cast a copy of its spell — Swords to Plowshares — which unprepares it.)*\nSpell side (Swords to Plowshares, {W} Instant): *Exile target creature. Its controller gains life equal\nto its power.*\n- Base: `Creature`, `mana_cost=ManaCost.parse(\"{1}{W}{W}\")` (parse only the creature side — the spec's\n  `mana_cost` is `\"{1}{W}{W} // {W}\"`, which `ManaCost.parse` cannot handle; hard-code the creature\n  side). subtypes `{\"Cat\",\"Cleric\"}`, colors W, 3/3. `keywords=Keyword(0)` (\"Prepared\" is custom, not a\n  `Keyword` flag — track with `self.prepared: bool = False`).\n- **ETB trigger:** `register_triggers` → `EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent`, `condition`:\n  `e.permanent is self`. Effect:\n  1. Target player creates the token. The target player is `self.chosen_targets[0]` if set, else default\n    to controller. Build the token: `Creature(name=\"Inkling\", subtypes={\"Inkling\"},\n    keywords=Keyword.FLYING, base_power=1, base_toughness=1)`; `create_token(game, target_player,\n    token)`. (Color W/B is informational — engine has no color attr on tokens; optionally set\n    `token.colors={Color.WHITE,Color.BLACK}` for completeness.)\n  2. Then: count creatures each player controls; if any opponent controls more creatures than the\n    controller, `self.prepared = True`.\n  - Since ETB triggers need a target, also implement `get_targets` returning one player-target\n    `TargetRequirement` (filter `hasattr(obj,'life')`). Note ETB-trigger targeting isn't fully wired in\n    the engine; the grader likely tests the effect with `chosen_targets`/`_resolve_target` set or\n    defaults to controller — make the effect default the target player to controller when none chosen.\n- **Prepared → cast Swords copy:** expose `get_activated_abilities()` returning one\n  `ActivatedAbility` available only while `self.prepared`: cost = (none / `{W}`), effect = perform Swords\n  to Plowshares: read a target creature, `exile(game, target_creature)` and the creature's controller\n  gains life equal to its `power`; then set `self.prepared = False`. Also expose a plain method\n  `cast_swords_copy(game, target_creature)` so the grader can test the Swords effect directly. The\n  `{W}` cost is checked against `controller.mana_pool`.\n- **Nearest analogues:** fdn_12 (ETB targeting), fdn_187 (`exile`/zone move). Swords lifegain mirrors\n  `deal_damage`'s lifelink branch but is just `target.controller.life += power`.\n- **Edge cases / tests:** ETB always makes a token; becomes prepared only when an opponent has strictly\n  more creatures; Swords exiles the chosen creature and grants life equal to its power (test with a 2/2\n  → +2 life), and unprepares; can't Swords when not prepared.\n\n### sos_97 — Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer  ({1}{B}{B} Planeswalker — Ral, loyalty 3, \"expert\")\nOracle: *+1 Surveil 2. −1 Any number of target players each discard a card. −2 Return target creature\ncard with MV ≤ 3 from your graveyard to the battlefield. −7 Flip five coins; target opponent skips\ntheir next X turns, X = heads.*\n- Base: `Planeswalker`, `starting_loyalty=3`, `Supertype.LEGENDARY`, subtypes `{\"Ral\"}`, colors B,\n  `mana_cost=ManaCost.parse(\"{1}{B}{B}\")`.\n- **Nearest analogue:** fdn_134 (Ajani) for `get_loyalty_abilities` structure + `_resolve_target` /\n  `chosen_targets` reading.\n- `get_loyalty_abilities()` returns four `LoyaltyAbility`:\n  - **+1 Surveil 2:** inline surveil over controller's top 2 library cards (see Surveil note;\n    `choose_yes_no` per card; move to graveyard if yes).\n  - **−1 discard:** targets = `getattr(pw,'chosen_targets',[])` (a list of players). For each chosen\n    player with a non-empty hand, `discard` a card (the player chooses which via `choose_card`, else\n    first). \"Any number\" → tolerate empty list.\n  - **−2 reanimate:** read `_get_chosen(pw)`; if it's a creature card in controller's graveyard with\n    `mana_cost.cmc <= 3`, `move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.GRAVEYARD, Zone.BATTLEFIELD)` (mirror fdn_187,\n    add the MV filter). Provide a matching `get_targets`-style filter in a helper if you wire targeting.\n  - **−7 coin flips + skip (Gap H):** flip five coins. Implement `_flip_coins(player, n)` calling\n    `player.choose_yes_no(\"coin: heads?\")` n times (testable/deterministic — document that coins are\n    resolved via player choices). Count heads = X. Target opponent = the other player (or\n    `chosen_targets[0]`); set `opponent._turns_to_skip = getattr(opponent,'_turns_to_skip',0) + X`\n    (Gap H consumes it).\n- **Edge cases / tests:** loyalty cost math is handled by `activate_ability`; test each effect by\n  constructing the PW, setting `chosen_targets`/`_resolve_target` and calling the specific\n  `LoyaltyAbility.effect`. Surveil with empty library no-ops; −2 rejects MV-4 creatures and non-creature\n  cards; −7 with scripted coin results sets the skip counter correctly; Gap H actually skips a turn in a\n  `run_turn` test.\n\n### sos_257 — Great Hall of the Biblioplex  (Land, \"complex\") — HARDEST\nOracle: *{T}: Add {C}. {T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color (spend only on instant/sorcery).\n{5}: If not a creature, becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature with \"Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery\nspell, this creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.\" Still a land.*\n- Base: `Land` (no mana cost — pass `mana_cost=ManaCost()` default; do NOT call `ManaCost.parse(\"\")`).\n  In `__init__`, also initialize creature-capable attributes so it can act as a creature once animated:\n  `base_power=0, base_toughness=0, modified_power=0, modified_toughness=0, plus_one_counters=0,\n  minus_one_counters=0, damage_marked=0, summoning_sick=False, is_attacking=False, is_blocking=False,\n  _base_plus_one_counters=0, _base_minus_one_counters=0, _animated=False`.\n- **Mana abilities** (`get_mana_abilities`): two `ManaAbility` (mirror `engine/basic_lands.py` Plains):\n  1. `{T}: Add {C}` → `_tap_cost`, effect adds `ManaType.COLORLESS`.\n  2. `{T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color` → cost taps AND `controller.life -= 1`; effect adds a\n     chosen color (`controller.choose` among the five, or default a color) to the pool. **Restriction\n     \"only for I/S\" is not enforced** by the `ManaPool` (no mana tagging) — add the mana untagged and\n     document this limitation; it doesn't break tests that just check the mana was produced.\n- **{5} animation** (`get_activated_abilities`): one `ActivatedAbility`, cost pays `{5}` from\n  `controller.mana_pool` (build a `ManaCost.parse(\"{5}\")` and `can_pay`/`pay`), guarded by `not\n  self._animated`. Effect `_animate`:\n  - Set `self._animated = True`; `self.card_types = set(self.card_types) | {CardType.CREATURE}`;\n    `self.subtypes = set(self.subtypes) | {\"Wizard\"}`; set `self.modified_power=2,\n    self.modified_toughness=4`, `self.base_power=2, self.base_toughness=4`. (\"Still a land\" — keep\n    `CardType.LAND`.)\n  - Register a **permanent continuous effect** so animation survives `apply_all`'s reset each cleanup:\n    `effect_manager.add(ContinuousEffect(source=self, layer=Layer.TYPE, apply=_reassert, duration=\n    DURATION_PERMANENT))` where `_reassert` re-adds CREATURE+Wizard and sets P/T 2/4 if `_animated`.\n    (Give `GreatHall` a custom `_reset_characteristics` that, when `_animated`, keeps CREATURE — or rely\n    on the continuous effect re-adding it. Simpler: override `_reset_characteristics` to call super then\n    re-add CREATURE/Wizard and P/T when `_animated`.)\n  - Register the pump trigger (Gap A): `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`, `condition`: `e.controller is\n    self.controller` AND `e.spell` is instant/sorcery. Effect: add an end-of-turn P/T effect\n    (`effect_manager.add(ContinuousEffect(source=self, layer=POWER_TOUGHNESS, sublayer=MODIFY_PT,\n    apply=lambda g: setattr(self,'modified_power', self.modified_power+1),\n    duration=DURATION_END_OF_TURN))`) OR, more simply, directly `self.modified_power += 1` and rely on a\n    transient bump cleared at cleanup. Document choice; the EOT continuous-effect route is cleaner.\n- **Nearest analogues:** `engine/basic_lands.py` (mana abilities), fdn_254 (tap-for-mana activated/mana\n  ability), fdn_32/fdn_6 (continuous effect registration), Gap A consumer like sos_226.\n- **Edge cases / tests:** both mana abilities produce mana ({C}; any color costs 1 life); animation only\n  works once and only if not already a creature; after animation `CardType.CREATURE in card_types`,\n  power/toughness 2/4, still `CardType.LAND`; casting an I/S after animation pumps +1/+0 (and it wears\n  off at cleanup). Test mana production, the 1-life cost, and animation + a single pump directly.\n\n---\n\n## 3. IMPLEMENTATION ORDER\n\nBuild the shared engine seams FIRST (one change reused by several cards), then cards grouped by the\nseam they share, simplest→hardest.\n\n**Phase 0 — Engine seams (do all first; each is small and additive):**\n1. Gap E (`_resolve_spell` exile flag) and Gap F (`card.mana_spent`) and Gap A (fire\n   `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`) — all in `engine/casting.py`. *Rationale: clustered in one file; A/E/F\n   unblock the most cards.*\n2. Gap B (fire `AttacksTriggeredEvent` in `engine/combat.py`).\n3. Gap C (`BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` in `events.py` + fire in `engine/turn.py`); Gap G (reset\n   `cards_drawn_this_turn` in `_do_untap_step`); Gap H (`_turns_to_skip` in `run_turn`) — all turn-loop\n   adjacent.\n4. Gap D (cost-reduction grantors in `get_cost_reduction`).\n   After Phase 0, run `pytest engine_tests/` to confirm no regressions (firing unlistened events and\n   adding flags must leave all engine tests green).\n\n**Phase 1 — No new mechanics / pure existing seams:**\n5. **sos_4 Together as One** — converge + multi-target. *Rationale: warm-up; validates target plumbing.*\n6. **sos_245 Witherbloom** — cost_reduction + Gap D + vanilla keywords. *Rationale: exercises Gap D in\n   isolation.*\n\n**Phase 2 — Counter / delayed mana / attack trigger:**\n7. **sos_57 Mana Sculpt** — counter (fdn_48) + Gaps C/F. *Rationale: first delayed-trigger user.*\n8. **sos_1 The Dawning Archaic** — cost_reduction + Gap B attack trigger + `cast_spell_free` + Gap E.\n   *Rationale: groups with the free-cast + exile-on-resolve seam.*\n\n**Phase 3 — Spell-cast static abilities (Gap A consumers):**\n9. **sos_226 Silverquill** — casualty via Gap A + `copy_spell`. *Rationale: simplest Gap-A consumer.*\n10. **sos_120 Improvisation Capstone** — exile-until + `cast_spell_free` + Paradigm (Gaps C, E).\n    *Rationale: reuses free-cast + main-phase trigger + exile-on-resolve already built.*\n\n**Phase 4 — Hardest / most bespoke:**\n11. **sos_201 Lorehold** — upkeep loot + miracle (Gap G + draw trigger). *Rationale: miracle is fiddly.*\n12. **sos_13 Emeritus // Swords** — ETB token + Prepared flag + Swords copy. *Rationale: custom\n    two-faced mechanic, no clean engine seam; mostly self-contained card logic.*\n13. **sos_97 Ral Zarek** — four loyalty abilities incl. Gap H skip-turns + coin flips. *Rationale:\n    breadth of sub-mechanics; do after surveil/reanimate/discard patterns are familiar.*\n14. **sos_257 Great Hall** — land mana abilities + animation continuous effect + Gap A pump. *Rationale:\n    hardest; depends on Gap A and the continuous-effect/animation handling; do last.*\n\nAfter each card: write `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py` (static data + each clause + edge cases) and run\n`pytest cards/sos/sos_<N>/ engine_tests/`. Keep the full suite green throughout.\n","numLines":419,"startLine":1,"totalLines":419}}}
