{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - Phase 2 (IMPLEMENTATION, TDD, requirements-driven) of a two-phase task. A planning agent wrote `/workspace/PLAN.md`.\n   - **Implement 10 SOS Magic: The Gathering cards: 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257** in `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_<N>/card_impl.py`. Each directory has a `card_spec.json` (source of truth, with `oracle_text`) and a `card_impl.py` template stub to fill in.\n   - Use completed FDN cards in `/workspace/cards/fdn/` as examples; refer to `RULEBOOK.txt` for deep rules.\n   - The contract is the **requirements (card_spec.json + RULEBOOK.txt), NOT the plan**. The plan is a guide/hypothesis from an agent that couldn't run code; verify every claim against the real engine and deviate when better (noting deviations in PLAN.md).\n   - Use TDD: one vertical tracer-bullet test at a time through the public interface (`test_utils`), watch it fail, write minimal code to pass. Don't write all tests up front. Write own tests in `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py` (max 30/card).\n   - Expected to make engine changes to implement new keywords/mechanics; MAY add files/methods/classes to `engine/` and edit existing function bodies, but MUST NOT rename/move/delete existing things.\n   - **CONSTRAINT (verbatim): \"Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading. Modifying the workspace tests will not change your score — it will only mislead you about whether your engine changes are correct.\"**\n   - After each card and after any engine/ change, run `python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ -q` — never ship a change that regresses it.\n   - Validate finished cards against requirements via a throwaway real-engine smoke check (not just tests).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Card base classes (engine/card.py): CardImpl, Creature, Instant, Sorcery, Enchantment, Aura, Artifact, ArtifactCreature, Planeswalker, Land. Kwargs use `.setdefault(...)` pattern in FDN cards.\n   - Hooks: `can_cast`, `cost_reduction(game)->int` (generic-only, clamped), `on_cast`, `on_resolve`, `get_targets`, `register_triggers`, `register_replacement_effects`, `get_activated_abilities`, `get_modes`, `Planeswalker.get_loyalty_abilities`, `Land.get_mana_abilities`.\n   - Targets: cast_spell stores chosen targets on StackObject.targets; _resolve_spell sets `card.chosen_targets`. FDN helper pattern: `_get_chosen_target` reads `chosen_targets` then falls back to `_resolve_target` test backdoor.\n   - TargetRequirement(filter_fn, description, zone) — filter_fn evaluated at cast; zone is informational (DeterministicPlayer returns scripted targets).\n   - Two ContinuousEffect classes — MUST import the real one from `engine.continuous_effects` (source, layer, sublayer, apply, timestamp, duration). `game.effect_manager.add(...)`. Layer IntEnum (TYPE=4, ABILITY=6, POWER_TOUGHNESS=7), SubLayer.MODIFY_PT, DURATION_PERMANENT=-1, DURATION_END_OF_TURN=0. apply_all only called during cleanup and resets characteristics first.\n   - Triggers: TriggerRegistration; effect(game) gets NO event — capture data in condition (stash on source) or peek stack. move_to_zone auto registers/unregisters triggers on battlefield entry/exit.\n   - cast_spell_free(game, player, card, from_zone) — free cast from any zone. copy_spell(game, stack_obj, controller, new_targets) for casualty.\n   - DeterministicPlayer: choose/choose_target/choose_yes_no/choose_card/assign_damage_order all pop from script deque.\n   - test_utils.cast_spell resolves stack LIFO (cast-trigger pushed above spell resolves first). set_board_state(battlefield=/hand=/graveyard=/life=/mana=). No set_library — must add directly to `player.zones[Zone.LIBRARY]`.\n   - Converge: cast_spell sets `card.colors_spent = list(mana_pool.last_payment_colors)`; fdn_205 sets int. Code must handle both: `len(cs) if isinstance(cs, list) else (cs or 0)`.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `/workspace/PLAN.md` — 418-line plan. Engine gaps A-H table and per-card plans. Reference, not spec.\n   - `/workspace/engine/casting.py` — MODIFIED (Gaps A, D, E, F):\n     - In cast_spell after `player.mana_pool.pay(effective_cost)`: added `card.mana_spent = effective_cost.cmc` (Gap F).\n     - At end of cast_spell after push: added `from engine.events import SpellCastTriggeredEvent; game.trigger_manager.fire_event(game, SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell=card, card=card, player=player, controller=player))` (Gap A).\n     - Same fire added at end of cast_spell_free (Gap A).\n     - In _resolve_spell non-permanent branch: `dest = Zone.EXILE if getattr(card, \"_exile_on_resolve\", False) else Zone.GRAVEYARD; move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.STACK, dest)` (Gap E).\n     - In get_cost_reduction: after `raw = card.cost_reduction(game)`, added a loop over `game.get_battlefield(controller).get_all()` (skip `perm is card`) summing `perm.grant_cost_reduction(game, card)` via getattr/callable into `granted`; return `max(0, min(raw + granted, generic))` (Gap D).\n   - `/workspace/engine/events.py` — MODIFIED: added after BeginningOfCombatTriggeredEvent:\n     ```python\n     @dataclass\n     class BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(TriggeredEvent):\n         player: Any = None\n         is_first_main: bool = False\n     ```\n   - `/workspace/engine/turn.py` — MODIFIED (Gaps G, H, C):\n     - In _do_untap_step after `active.land_plays_remaining = 1`: `for player in game.players: player.cards_drawn_this_turn = 0` (Gap G).\n     - At top of run_turn before `start_turn`: `active = game.active_player; if getattr(active, \"_turns_to_skip\", 0) > 0: active._turns_to_skip -= 1; skip_start = game.turn_number; while game.turn_number == skip_start: game.advance_phase(); return` (Gap H).\n     - Added elif branches firing BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent for `(Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN, None)` with is_first_main=True and `(Phase.POSTCOMBAT_MAIN, None)` with is_first_main=False (Gap C).\n   - `/workspace/engine/combat.py` — MODIFIED (Gap B): in declare_attackers_step, added `declared: list[Any] = []`, append each attacker after tapping, then after loop: `from engine.events import AttacksTriggeredEvent; for attacker in declared: game.trigger_manager.fire_event(game, AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature=attacker, attacker=attacker))`.\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_4/card_impl.py` — CREATED. TogetherAsOne(Sorcery), mana_cost {6}. Has `_colors_spent_count(card)` helper, `_is_any_target(obj)` helper. get_targets returns 2 TargetRequirements (player, any target). on_resolve: x = colors spent; chosen_targets[0] draws x via draw_card, deal_damage(game, self, chosen[1], x), controller.life += x.\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_4/tests.py` — CREATED. Tests: static data, X=2 draws/damages/gains, damage to player, X=0 no-op, real_cast_converge (mana W:3 U:3 paying {6} → X=2). Uses `_dummy_library` helper adding Creatures to `player.zones[Zone.LIBRARY]`.\n   - FDN reference patterns studied: fdn_205 (converge, sets self.colors_spent int), fdn_212 (two targets via _get_chosen_target_idx), fdn_48 Refute (_counter_spell removes from `game.stack._items`, moves card to graveyard; can_cast checks stack.objects()), fdn_6 ClawsOut (cost_reduction counts subtypes, continuous effect end-of-turn buff), fdn_134 Ajani (get_loyalty_abilities returns LoyaltyAbility list, reads `_resolve_target`), fdn_187 Zombify (graveyard→battlefield via move_to_zone), fdn_32 (surveil inline via library.top + choose_yes_no, continuous effect Layer.ABILITY DURATION_PERMANENT).\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - Write tool rejected on sos_4/card_impl.py with \"File has not been read yet. Read it first before writing to it.\" Fixed by reading the file first, then re-issuing the Write (succeeded). NOTE: the harness requires reading a file before Write even when the template content is already visible in conversation.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Identified that the plan's `ContinuousEffect(source, layer, sublayer, apply, timestamp, duration)` references the one in `engine/continuous_effects.py`, NOT the stub in `engine/card.py`. Must import from continuous_effects.\n   - Confirmed Phase 0 event-firing additions are safe (no listeners → fire_event no-ops); verified via grep no existing engine code/tests use the new attributes.\n   - All 1145 engine tests pass after Phase 0 changes.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - (System-reminder listing deferred tools and skills available.)\n   - Main task message: \"Phase 2 of 2 — IMPLEMENTATION (TDD, requirements-driven)\" with full contract: implement SOS cards 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257; use FDN examples; RULEBOOK.txt; engine API discovery via source docstrings; \"You are expected to make changes to the engine to implement new keywords and mechanics.\" Constraint: **\"Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading. Modifying the workspace tests will not change your score — it will only mislead you about whether your engine changes are correct.\"**\n   - Final message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools\" — requesting this conversation summary.\n   - (Multiple system-reminders nudging use of TaskCreate/TaskUpdate, and one \"Tool loaded.\" after ToolSearch.)\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Task #2 sos_4 Together as One (in_progress — code written, tests written, tests NOT yet run)\n   - Task #3 sos_245 Witherbloom (Elder Dragon, affinity for creatures self + granted to I/S via grant_cost_reduction/Gap D)\n   - Task #4 sos_57 Mana Sculpt (counter + delayed mana via Gap C/F, Wizard check)\n   - Task #5 sos_1 The Dawning Archaic (cost reduction by graveyard I/S, Gap