{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CJN82RdFN3Y5oqTggquHBR","type":"tool_result","content":"218\t### sos_120 — Improvisation Capstone  ({5}{R}{R} Sorcery — Lesson, \"complex\")\n219\tOracle: *Exile cards from top of library until total mana value ≥ 4; you may cast any number of them\n220\twithout paying mana costs. Paradigm (exile this spell; after you first resolve a spell with this name,\n221\tat the beginning of each of your first main phases you may cast a copy of it from exile without paying\n222\tits mana cost).*\n223\t- Base: `Sorcery`, subtypes `{\"Lesson\"}`.\n224\t- **Main effect `on_resolve`:**\n225\t  1. Exile from top of controller's library (use `library.top(1)` repeatedly, `move_to_zone(...\n226\t     LIBRARY, EXILE)`) accumulating `mana_cost.cmc`, until total ≥ 4 or library empty. Track the exiled\n227\t     cards.\n228\t  2. For each exiled **castable** card (not a land; has a non-empty mana cost as appropriate), ask\n229\t     `choose_yes_no`; if yes, `cast_spell_free(game, controller, card, Zone.EXILE)`. \"Any number\" — loop\n230\t     over the exiled set. (Resolve each before moving on; in tests resolution is immediate.)\n231\t- **Paradigm:** set `self._exile_on_resolve = True` (Gap E) so the Capstone itself is exiled rather\n232\t  than going to the graveyard after it resolves. Also register a recurring trigger (Gap C) on\n233\t  `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`, `condition=lambda g,e: e.player is controller and\n234\t  e.is_first_main`, effect: if a copy can be cast, `choose_yes_no` then **cast a copy from exile** —\n235\t  implement as: shallow-copy this card (or re-cast the exiled card) via `cast_spell_free` from\n236\t  `Zone.EXILE` — but \"cast a copy\" means the original stays in exile. Simplest faithful approach: build\n237\t  a copy object (`copy.copy(self)`), give it owner/controller, and `cast_spell_free(game, controller,\n238\t  the_copy, Zone.EXILE)` after temporarily placing the copy in exile; the copy resolves and is exiled\n239\t  again (harmless) or just let it go to graveyard. **Document the simplification you choose.**\n240\t  - \"After you first resolve a spell with this name\" — register the recurring trigger inside\n241\t    `on_resolve` (i.e., the first resolution arms Paradigm). Keep it simple: arm once.\n242\t- **Nearest analogues:** fdn_187/`cast_spell_free` for free casts from exile.\n243\t- **Edge cases / tests:** exile stops as soon as total MV ≥ 4 (e.g., one MV-4 card stops immediately);\n244\t  lands among exiled cards can't be cast (skip); empty library → no exiles; the Capstone ends in exile\n245\t  (Gap E). Test the exile-until loop and a single free cast directly. The recurring Paradigm copy can be\n246\t  tested by firing the main-phase event once with the Capstone in exile.\n247\t\n248\t### sos_201 — Lorehold, the Historian  ({3}{R}{W} 5/5 Elder Dragon, \"expert\")\n249\tOracle: *Flying, haste. Each instant/sorcery card in your hand has miracle {2}. At the beginning of\n250\teach opponent's upkeep, you may discard a card; if you do, draw a card.*\n251\t- Base: `Creature`, `keywords=Keyword.FLYING|Keyword.HASTE`, `{\"Elder\",\"Dragon\"}`, LEGENDARY, 5/5.\n252\t- **Opponent-upkeep loot:** `register_triggers` → `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` (fired with no\n253\t  player; check `game.active_player is not self.controller`). Effect: if controller has ≥1 card in\n254\t  hand, `choose_yes_no`; if yes, pick a card → `discard(game, controller, card)` then\n255\t  `draw_card(game, controller)`.\n256\t- **Miracle {2} (Gap G + draw trigger):** `register_triggers` → `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent`,\n257\t  `condition`: `e.player is self.controller` AND drawn `e.card` is instant/sorcery AND it's the first\n258\t  card drawn this turn (`getattr(e.player,'cards_drawn_this_turn',0) == 1` — Gap G makes this reset per\n259\t  turn; `draw_card` increments before firing). Effect `_miracle`: ask `choose_yes_no(\"cast <card> for\n260\t  miracle {2}?\")`; if yes and `controller.mana_pool.can_pay(ManaCost.parse(\"{2}\"))`, pay it and\n261\t  `cast_spell_free(game, controller, e.card_FROM_CONDITION, Zone.HAND)`. Because the effect gets no\n262\t  event, stash the drawn card on `self._miracle_card` in the condition and read it in the effect; clear"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d616a92e-14a8-4e9f-8780-afe29cd109e3","uuid":"3c976ff8-568f-4aab-b3b5-e51c3b977b57","timestamp":"2026-06-04T09:10:54.999Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/PLAN.md","content":"### sos_120 — Improvisation Capstone  ({5}{R}{R} Sorcery — Lesson, \"complex\")\nOracle: *Exile cards from top of library until total mana value ≥ 4; you may cast any number of them\nwithout paying mana costs. Paradigm (exile this spell; after you first resolve a spell with this name,\nat the beginning of each of your first main phases you may cast a copy of it from exile without paying\nits mana cost).*\n- Base: `Sorcery`, subtypes `{\"Lesson\"}`.\n- **Main effect `on_resolve`:**\n  1. Exile from top of controller's library (use `library.top(1)` repeatedly, `move_to_zone(...\n     LIBRARY, EXILE)`) accumulating `mana_cost.cmc`, until total ≥ 4 or library empty. Track the exiled\n     cards.\n  2. For each exiled **castable** card (not a land; has a non-empty mana cost as appropriate), ask\n     `choose_yes_no`; if yes, `cast_spell_free(game, controller, card, Zone.EXILE)`. \"Any number\" — loop\n     over the exiled set. (Resolve each before moving on; in tests resolution is immediate.)\n- **Paradigm:** set `self._exile_on_resolve = True` (Gap E) so the Capstone itself is exiled rather\n  than going to the graveyard after it resolves. Also register a recurring trigger (Gap C) on\n  `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`, `condition=lambda g,e: e.player is controller and\n  e.is_first_main`, effect: if a copy can be cast, `choose_yes_no` then **cast a copy from exile** —\n  implement as: shallow-copy this card (or re-cast the exiled card) via `cast_spell_free` from\n  `Zone.EXILE` — but \"cast a copy\" means the original stays in exile. Simplest faithful approach: build\n  a copy object (`copy.copy(self)`), give it owner/controller, and `cast_spell_free(game, controller,\n  the_copy, Zone.EXILE)` after temporarily placing the copy in exile; the copy resolves and is exiled\n  again (harmless) or just let it go to graveyard. **Document the simplification you choose.**\n  - \"After you first resolve a spell with this name\" — register the recurring trigger inside\n    `on_resolve` (i.e., the first resolution arms Paradigm). Keep it simple: arm once.\n- **Nearest analogues:** fdn_187/`cast_spell_free` for free casts from exile.\n- **Edge cases / tests:** exile stops as soon as total MV ≥ 4 (e.g., one MV-4 card stops immediately);\n  lands among exiled cards can't be cast (skip); empty library → no exiles; the Capstone ends in exile\n  (Gap E). Test the exile-until loop and a single free cast directly. The recurring Paradigm copy can be\n  tested by firing the main-phase event once with the Capstone in exile.\n\n### sos_201 — Lorehold, the Historian  ({3}{R}{W} 5/5 Elder Dragon, \"expert\")\nOracle: *Flying, haste. Each instant/sorcery card in your hand has miracle {2}. At the beginning of\neach opponent's upkeep, you may discard a card; if you do, draw a card.*\n- Base: `Creature`, `keywords=Keyword.FLYING|Keyword.HASTE`, `{\"Elder\",\"Dragon\"}`, LEGENDARY, 5/5.\n- **Opponent-upkeep loot:** `register_triggers` → `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` (fired with no\n  player; check `game.active_player is not self.controller`). Effect: if controller has ≥1 card in\n  hand, `choose_yes_no`; if yes, pick a card → `discard(game, controller, card)` then\n  `draw_card(game, controller)`.\n- **Miracle {2} (Gap G + draw trigger):** `register_triggers` → `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent`,\n  `condition`: `e.player is self.controller` AND drawn `e.card` is instant/sorcery AND it's the first\n  card drawn this turn (`getattr(e.player,'cards_drawn_this_turn',0) == 1` — Gap G makes this reset per\n  turn; `draw_card` increments before firing). Effect `_miracle`: ask `choose_yes_no(\"cast <card> for\n  miracle {2}?\")`; if yes and `controller.mana_pool.can_pay(ManaCost.parse(\"{2}\"))`, pay it and\n  `cast_spell_free(game, controller, e.card_FROM_CONDITION, Zone.HAND)`. Because the effect gets no\n  event, stash the drawn card on `self._miracle_card` in the condition and read it in the effect; clear","numLines":45,"startLine":218,"totalLines":419}}}
