{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - Phase 2 of 2 — IMPLEMENTATION (TDD, requirements-driven). A planning agent wrote `/workspace/PLAN.md`.\n   - **Implement 10 SOS Magic: The Gathering cards: 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257** in `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_<N>/card_impl.py`. Each dir has a `card_spec.json` (source of truth, with `oracle_text`) and a `card_impl.py` template stub to fill in.\n   - Use completed FDN cards in `/workspace/cards/fdn/` as examples; refer to `RULEBOOK.txt` for deep rules. The contract is the requirements (card_spec.json + RULEBOOK.txt), NOT the plan. The plan is a guide/hypothesis; verify every claim against the real engine and deviate when better (noting deviations in PLAN.md).\n   - Use TDD: write one vertical tracer-bullet test at a time through the public interface (`test_utils`), watch it fail, write minimal code to pass. Don't write all tests up front. Own tests go in `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py` (max 30/card).\n   - Expected to make engine changes for new keywords/mechanics; MAY add files/methods/classes to `engine/` and edit existing function bodies, but MUST NOT rename/move/delete existing things.\n   - After each card and after any engine/ change, run `python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ -q` — never ship a change that regresses it. Also run `pytest cards/sos/sos_<N>/ engine_tests/` after each card. Keep the full suite green throughout.\n   - Validate finished cards against requirements via a throwaway real-engine smoke check (not just tests).\n   - **CONSTRAINT (verbatim): \"Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading. Modifying the workspace tests will not change your