{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S44Gb84TTr7jF9wPqnJ2Q8","type":"tool_result","content":"305\t### sos_97 — Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer  ({1}{B}{B} Planeswalker — Ral, loyalty 3, \"expert\")\n306\tOracle: *+1 Surveil 2. −1 Any number of target players each discard a card. −2 Return target creature\n307\tcard with MV ≤ 3 from your graveyard to the battlefield. −7 Flip five coins; target opponent skips\n308\ttheir next X turns, X = heads.*\n309\t- Base: `Planeswalker`, `starting_loyalty=3`, `Supertype.LEGENDARY`, subtypes `{\"Ral\"}`, colors B,\n310\t  `mana_cost=ManaCost.parse(\"{1}{B}{B}\")`.\n311\t- **Nearest analogue:** fdn_134 (Ajani) for `get_loyalty_abilities` structure + `_resolve_target` /\n312\t  `chosen_targets` reading.\n313\t- `get_loyalty_abilities()` returns four `LoyaltyAbility`:\n314\t  - **+1 Surveil 2:** inline surveil over controller's top 2 library cards (see Surveil note;\n315\t    `choose_yes_no` per card; move to graveyard if yes).\n316\t  - **−1 discard:** targets = `getattr(pw,'chosen_targets',[])` (a list of players). For each chosen\n317\t    player with a non-empty hand, `discard` a card (the player chooses which via `choose_card`, else\n318\t    first). \"Any number\" → tolerate empty list.\n319\t  - **−2 reanimate:** read `_get_chosen(pw)`; if it's a creature card in controller's graveyard with\n320\t    `mana_cost.cmc <= 3`, `move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.GRAVEYARD, Zone.BATTLEFIELD)` (mirror fdn_187,\n321\t    add the MV filter). Provide a matching `get_targets`-style filter in a helper if you wire targeting.\n322\t  - **−7 coin flips + skip (Gap H):** flip five coins. Implement `_flip_coins(player, n)` calling\n323\t    `player.choose_yes_no(\"coin: heads?\")` n times (testable/deterministic — document that coins are\n324\t    resolved via player choices). Count heads = X. Target opponent = the other player (or\n325\t    `chosen_targets[0]`); set `opponent._turns_to_skip = getattr(opponent,'_turns_to_skip',0) + X`\n326\t    (Gap H consumes it).\n327\t- **Edge cases / tests:** loyalty cost math is handled by `activate_ability`; test each effect by\n328\t  constructing the PW, setting `chosen_targets`/`_resolve_target` and calling the specific\n329\t  `LoyaltyAbility.effect`. Surveil with empty library no-ops; −2 rejects MV-4 creatures and non-creature\n330\t  cards; −7 with scripted coin results sets the skip counter correctly; Gap H actually skips a turn in a\n331\t  `run_turn` test.\n332\t\n333\t### sos_257 — Great Hall of the Biblioplex  (Land, \"complex\") — HARDEST\n334\tOracle: *{T}: Add {C}. {T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color (spend only on instant/sorcery).\n335\t{5}: If not a creature, becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature with \"Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery\n336\tspell, this creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.\" Still a land.*\n337\t- Base: `Land` (no mana cost — pass `mana_cost=ManaCost()` default; do NOT call `ManaCost.parse(\"\")`).\n338\t  In `__init__`, also initialize creature-capable attributes so it can act as a creature once animated:\n339\t  `base_power=0, base_toughness=0, modified_power=0, modified_toughness=0, plus_one_counters=0,\n340\t  minus_one_counters=0, damage_marked=0, summoning_sick=False, is_attacking=False, is_blocking=False,\n341\t  _base_plus_one_counters=0, _base_minus_one_counters=0, _animated=False`.\n342\t- **Mana abilities** (`get_mana_abilities`): two `ManaAbility` (mirror `engine/basic_lands.py` Plains):\n343\t  1. `{T}: Add {C}` → `_tap_cost`, effect adds `ManaType.COLORLESS`.\n344\t  2. `{T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color` → cost taps AND `controller.life -= 1`; effect adds a\n345\t     chosen color (`controller.choose` among the five, or default a color) to the pool. **Restriction\n346\t     \"only for I/S\" is not enforced** by the `ManaPool` (no mana tagging) — add the mana untagged and\n347\t     document this limitation; it doesn't break tests that just check the mana was produced.\n348\t- **{5} animation** (`get_activated_abilities`): one `ActivatedAbility`, cost pays `{5}` from\n349\t  `controller.mana_pool` (build a `ManaCost.parse(\"{5}\")` and `can_pay`/`pay`), guarded by `not\n350\t  self._animated`. Effect `_animate`:\n351\t  - Set `self._animated = True`; `self.card_types = set(self.card_types) | {CardType.CREATURE}`;\n352\t    `self.subtypes = set(self.subtypes) | {\"Wizard\"}`; set `self.modified_power=2,\n353\t    self.modified_toughness=4`, `self.base_power=2, self.base_toughness=4`. (\"Still a land\" — keep\n354\t    `CardType.LAND`.)\n355\t  - Register a **permanent continuous effect** so animation survives `apply_all`'s reset each cleanup:\n356\t    `effect_manager.add(ContinuousEffect(source=self, layer=Layer.TYPE, apply=_reassert, duration=\n357\t    DURATION_PERMANENT))` where `_reassert` re-adds CREATURE+Wizard and sets P/T 2/4 if `_animated`.\n358\t    (Give `GreatHall` a custom `_reset_characteristics` that, when `_animated`, keeps CREATURE — or rely\n359\t    on the continuous effect re-adding it. Simpler: override `_reset_characteristics` to call super then\n360\t    re-add CREATURE/Wizard and P/T when `_animated`.)\n361\t  - Register the pump trigger (Gap A): `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`, `condition`: `e.controller is\n362\t    self.controller` AND `e.spell` is instant/sorcery. Effect: add an end-of-turn P/T effect\n363\t    (`effect_manager.add(ContinuousEffect(source=self, layer=POWER_TOUGHNESS, sublayer=MODIFY_PT,\n364\t    apply=lambda g: setattr(self,'modified_power', self.modified_power+1),\n365\t    duration=DURATION_END_OF_TURN))`) OR, more simply, directly `self.modified_power += 1` and rely on a\n366\t    transient bump cleared at cleanup. Document choice; the EOT continuous-effect route is cleaner.\n367\t- **Nearest analogues:** `engine/basic_lands.py` (mana abilities), fdn_254 (tap-for-mana activated/mana\n368\t  ability), fdn_32/fdn_6 (continuous effect registration), Gap A consumer like sos_226.\n369\t- **Edge cases / tests:** both mana abilities produce mana ({C}; any color costs 1 life); animation only\n370\t  works once and only if not already a creature; after animation `CardType.CREATURE in card_types`,\n371\t  power/toughness 2/4, still `CardType.LAND`; casting an I/S after animation pumps +1/+0 (and it wears\n372\t  off at cleanup). Test mana production, the 1-life cost, and animation + a single pump directly.\n373\t\n374\t---\n375\t\n376\t## 3. IMPLEMENTATION ORDER\n377\t\n378\tBuild the shared engine seams FIRST (one change reused by several cards), then cards grouped by the\n379\tseam they share, simplest→hardest.\n380\t\n381\t**Phase 0 — Engine seams (do all first; each is small and additive):**\n382\t1. Gap E (`_resolve_spell` exile flag) and Gap F (`card.mana_spent`) and Gap A (fire\n383\t   `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`) — all in `engine/casting.py`. *Rationale: clustered in one file; A/E/F\n384\t   unblock the most cards.*\n385\t2. Gap B (fire `AttacksTriggeredEvent` in `engine/combat.py`).\n386\t3. Gap C (`BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` in `events.py` + fire in `engine/turn.py`); Gap G (reset\n387\t   `cards_drawn_this_turn` in `_do_untap_step`); Gap H (`_turns_to_skip` in `run_turn`) — all turn-loop\n388\t   adjacent.\n389\t4. Gap D (cost-reduction grantors in `get_cost_reduction`).\n390\t   After Phase 0, run `pytest engine_tests/` to confirm no regressions (firing unlistened events and\n391\t   adding flags must leave all engine tests green).\n392\t\n393\t**Phase 1 — No new mechanics / pure existing seams:**\n394\t5. **sos_4 Together as One** — converge + multi-target. *Rationale: warm-up; validates target plumbing.*"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d616a92e-14a8-4e9f-8780-afe29cd109e3","uuid":"9123d645-1e5b-404b-b4ab-98b86fb1b9f2","timestamp":"2026-06-04T09:23:40.876Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/PLAN.md","content":"### sos_97 — Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer  ({1}{B}{B} Planeswalker — Ral, loyalty 3, \"expert\")\nOracle: *+1 Surveil 2. −1 Any number of target players each discard a card. −2 Return target creature\ncard with MV ≤ 3 from your graveyard to the battlefield. −7 Flip five coins; target opponent skips\ntheir next X turns, X = heads.*\n- Base: `Planeswalker`, `starting_loyalty=3`, `Supertype.LEGENDARY`, subtypes `{\"Ral\"}`, colors B,\n  `mana_cost=ManaCost.parse(\"{1}{B}{B}\")`.\n- **Nearest analogue:** fdn_134 (Ajani) for `get_loyalty_abilities` structure + `_resolve_target` /\n  `chosen_targets` reading.\n- `get_loyalty_abilities()` returns four `LoyaltyAbility`:\n  - **+1 Surveil 2:** inline surveil over controller's top 2 library cards (see Surveil note;\n    `choose_yes_no` per card; move to graveyard if yes).\n  - **−1 discard:** targets = `getattr(pw,'chosen_targets',[])` (a list of players). For each chosen\n    player with a non-empty hand, `discard` a card (the player chooses which via `choose_card`, else\n    first). \"Any number\" → tolerate empty list.\n  - **−2 reanimate:** read `_get_chosen(pw)`; if it's a creature card in controller's graveyard with\n    `mana_cost.cmc <= 3`, `move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.GRAVEYARD, Zone.BATTLEFIELD)` (mirror fdn_187,\n    add the MV filter). Provide a matching `get_targets`-style filter in a helper if you wire targeting.\n  - **−7 coin flips + skip (Gap H):** flip five coins. Implement `_flip_coins(player, n)` calling\n    `player.choose_yes_no(\"coin: heads?\")` n times (testable/deterministic — document that coins are\n    resolved via player choices). Count heads = X. Target opponent = the other player (or\n    `chosen_targets[0]`); set `opponent._turns_to_skip = getattr(opponent,'_turns_to_skip',0) + X`\n    (Gap H consumes it).\n- **Edge cases / tests:** loyalty cost math is handled by `activate_ability`; test each effect by\n  constructing the PW, setting `chosen_targets`/`_resolve_target` and calling the specific\n  `LoyaltyAbility.effect`. Surveil with empty library no-ops; −2 rejects MV-4 creatures and non-creature\n  cards; −7 with scripted coin results sets the skip counter correctly; Gap H actually skips a turn in a\n  `run_turn` test.\n\n### sos_257 — Great Hall of the Biblioplex  (Land, \"complex\") — HARDEST\nOracle: *{T}: Add {C}. {T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color (spend only on instant/sorcery).\n{5}: If not a creature, becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature with \"Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery\nspell, this creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.\" Still a land.*\n- Base: `Land` (no mana cost — pass `mana_cost=ManaCost()` default; do NOT call `ManaCost.parse(\"\")`).\n  In `__init__`, also initialize creature-capable attributes so it can act as a creature once animated:\n  `base_power=0, base_toughness=0, modified_power=0, modified_toughness=0, plus_one_counters=0,\n  minus_one_counters=0, damage_marked=0, summoning_sick=False, is_attacking=False, is_blocking=False,\n  _base_plus_one_counters=0, _base_minus_one_counters=0, _animated=False`.\n- **Mana abilities** (`get_mana_abilities`): two `ManaAbility` (mirror `engine/basic_lands.py` Plains):\n  1. `{T}: Add {C}` → `_tap_cost`, effect adds `ManaType.COLORLESS`.\n  2. `{T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color` → cost taps AND `controller.life -= 1`; effect adds a\n     chosen color (`controller.choose` among the five, or default a color) to the pool. **Restriction\n     \"only for I/S\" is not enforced** by the `ManaPool` (no mana tagging) — add the mana untagged and\n     document this limitation; it doesn't break tests that just check the mana was produced.\n- **{5} animation** (`get_activated_abilities`): one `ActivatedAbility`, cost pays `{5}` from\n  `controller.mana_pool` (build a `ManaCost.parse(\"{5}\")` and `can_pay`/`pay`), guarded by `not\n  self._animated`. Effect `_animate`:\n  - Set `self._animated = True`; `self.card_types = set(self.card_types) | {CardType.CREATURE}`;\n    `self.subtypes = set(self.subtypes) | {\"Wizard\"}`; set `self.modified_power=2,\n    self.modified_toughness=4`, `self.base_power=2, self.base_toughness=4`. (\"Still a land\" — keep\n    `CardType.LAND`.)\n  - Register a **permanent continuous effect** so animation survives `apply_all`'s reset each cleanup:\n    `effect_manager.add(ContinuousEffect(source=self, layer=Layer.TYPE, apply=_reassert, duration=\n    DURATION_PERMANENT))` where `_reassert` re-adds CREATURE+Wizard and sets P/T 2/4 if `_animated`.\n    (Give `GreatHall` a custom `_reset_characteristics` that, when `_animated`, keeps CREATURE — or rely\n    on the continuous effect re-adding it. Simpler: override `_reset_characteristics` to call super then\n    re-add CREATURE/Wizard and P/T when `_animated`.)\n  - Register the pump trigger (Gap A): `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`, `condition`: `e.controller is\n    self.controller` AND `e.spell` is instant/sorcery. Effect: add an end-of-turn P/T effect\n    (`effect_manager.add(ContinuousEffect(source=self, layer=POWER_TOUGHNESS, sublayer=MODIFY_PT,\n    apply=lambda g: setattr(self,'modified_power', self.modified_power+1),\n    duration=DURATION_END_OF_TURN))`) OR, more simply, directly `self.modified_power += 1` and rely on a\n    transient bump cleared at cleanup. Document choice; the EOT continuous-effect route is cleaner.\n- **Nearest analogues:** `engine/basic_lands.py` (mana abilities), fdn_254 (tap-for-mana activated/mana\n  ability), fdn_32/fdn_6 (continuous effect registration), Gap A consumer like sos_226.\n- **Edge cases / tests:** both mana abilities produce mana ({C}; any color costs 1 life); animation only\n  works once and only if not already a creature; after animation `CardType.CREATURE in card_types`,\n  power/toughness 2/4, still `CardType.LAND`; casting an I/S after animation pumps +1/+0 (and it wears\n  off at cleanup). Test mana production, the 1-life cost, and animation + a single pump directly.\n\n---\n\n## 3. IMPLEMENTATION ORDER\n\nBuild the shared engine seams FIRST (one change reused by several cards), then cards grouped by the\nseam they share, simplest→hardest.\n\n**Phase 0 — Engine seams (do all first; each is small and additive):**\n1. Gap E (`_resolve_spell` exile flag) and Gap F (`card.mana_spent`) and Gap A (fire\n   `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`) — all in `engine/casting.py`. *Rationale: clustered in one file; A/E/F\n   unblock the most cards.*\n2. Gap B (fire `AttacksTriggeredEvent` in `engine/combat.py`).\n3. Gap C (`BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` in `events.py` + fire in `engine/turn.py`); Gap G (reset\n   `cards_drawn_this_turn` in `_do_untap_step`); Gap H (`_turns_to_skip` in `run_turn`) — all turn-loop\n   adjacent.\n4. Gap D (cost-reduction grantors in `get_cost_reduction`).\n   After Phase 0, run `pytest engine_tests/` to confirm no regressions (firing unlistened events and\n   adding flags must leave all engine tests green).\n\n**Phase 1 — No new mechanics / pure existing seams:**\n5. **sos_4 Together as One** — converge + multi-target. *Rationale: warm-up; validates target plumbing.*","numLines":90,"startLine":305,"totalLines":419}}}
