{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - Phase 2 of 2 — IMPLEMENTATION (TDD, requirements-driven). A planning agent wrote `/workspace/PLAN.md`.\n   - **Implement 10 SOS Magic: The Gathering cards: 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257** in `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_<N>/card_impl.py`. Each dir has `card_spec.json` (source of truth, with `oracle_text`) and a `card_impl.py` template stub to fill in.\n   - Use completed FDN cards in `/workspace/cards/fdn/` as examples; refer to `RULEBOOK.txt` for deep rules. The contract is the requirements (card_spec.json + RULEBOOK.txt), NOT the plan. The plan is a guide/hypothesis; verify every claim against the real engine and deviate when better (noting deviations in PLAN.md).\n   - Use TDD: write tests through the public interface (`test_utils`), watch them fail, write minimal code to pass. Own tests go in `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py` (max 30/card).\n   - MAY add files/methods/classes to `engine/` and edit existing function bodies, but MUST NOT rename/move/delete existing things.\n   - After each card run `python3 -m pytest cards/sos/sos_<N>/ engine_tests/` — never regress engine_tests; keep full suite green.\n   - Validate finished cards against requirements via a throwaway real-engine smoke check.\n   - **CONSTRAINT (verbatim): \"Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading. Modifying the workspace tests will not change your score — it will only mislead you about whether your engine changes are correct.\"**\n   - Final instruction (verbatim): \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" (requesting this summary).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Card base classes (engine/card.py): CardImpl, Creature, Instant, Sorcery, Enchantment, Aura, Artifact, ArtifactCreature, Planeswalker, Land. Kwargs use `.setdefault(...)`.\n   - Hooks: `can_cast`, `cost_reduction(game)->int`, `grant_cost_reduction(self, game, spell)->int`, `on_cast`, `on_resolve` (reads `self.chosen_targets`), `get_targets`, `register_triggers`, `get_activated_abilities()->list[ActivatedAbility]`, `Planeswalker.get_loyalty_abilities()->list[LoyaltyAbility]`, `Land.get_mana_abilities()->list[ManaAbility]`.\n   - `ActivatedAbility` (card.py dataclass): `cost: Callable`, `effect: Callable`, `description: str`. `cost(game, source)->bool`, `effect(game)->None`.\n   - `ManaAbility` (card.py dataclass): `cost`, `mana_produced`, `description`. Test by calling `ab.cost(game, card)` then `ab.mana_produced(game)` directly.\n   - `LoyaltyAbility` (card.py dataclass): `loyalty_cost: int`, `effect: Callable`, `description`.\n   - `ActivatedAbilityInstance` (engine/abilities.py): `source, controller, cost, effect, is_mana_ability=False, description`. `activate_ability(game, player, instance)` pays cost via `cost(game, source)`, then pushes StackObject (on_resolve=effect) if non-mana, or resolves immediately if mana ability. Loyalty abilities are sorcery-speed only, once/turn.\n   - Planeswalker: `starting_loyalty` kwarg, `self.loyalty`, `get_loyalty_abilities()`. Loyalty ability targets are NOT auto-set; effects read `pw.chosen_targets` (list) / `pw._resolve_target` (single).\n   - move_to_zone (engine/zones.py): on entering battlefield, registers triggers FIRST then fires EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent — so a normally-cast permanent's OWN self-ETB trigger (`register_triggers` + condition `e.permanent is source`) DOES catch its own entry (Angel of Finality pattern). NOTE: create_token fires ETB BEFORE registering token's own triggers (opposite). `_resolve_spell` calls `card.on_resolve(game)` then move_to_zone to battlefield (permanents) / graveyard-or-exile (non-perm via `_exile_on_resolve`).\n   - EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent(permanent, controller). SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell, card, player, controller). BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent(), DrawsCardTriggeredEvent(player, card), BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player, is_first_main).\n   - create_token(game, player, token): sets is_token=True, owner/controller=player, adds to battlefield, fires ETB.\n   - ZoneContainer: index 0=bottom, -1=top. `top(n)` returns last n (bottom-to-top order). `add(obj, position=\"top\")` appends (top); `position=\"bottom\"` inserts at 0. `get_all()` bottom→top, `contains`, `remove`, `__len__`.\n   - ManaType: WHITE=\"W\", BLUE=\"U\", BLACK=\"B\", RED=\"R\", GREEN=\"G\", COLORLESS=\"C\". ManaPool.can_pay/pay handle colored pips via `cost.pips` (need matching colored mana); generic paid by any. ManaCost.parse(\"{W}\"), `.cmc`, `.generic`, `.pips`.\n   - TargetRequirement(filter_fn, description, zone). Player targets: `filter_fn=lambda obj: hasattr(obj, \"life\")`.\n   - Continuous effects (engine/continuous_effects.py): `Layer` IntEnum (COPY=1,CONTROL=2,TEXT=3,TYPE=4,COLOR=5,ABILITY=6,POWER_TOUGHNESS=7); `SubLayer` (CHARACTERISTIC_DEFINING=\"7a\", SET_PT=\"7b\", MODIFY_PT=\"7c\", COUNTERS=\"7d\"); `ContinuousEffect(source, layer, sublayer=None, apply=Callable(game)->None, timestamp=0, duration=DURATION_PERMANENT(-1)/DURATION_END_OF_TURN(0)/positive-turn-number)`. `EffectManager` (game.effect_manager): add/remove/remove_expired/apply_all. apply_all calls `_reset_characteristics()` on all battlefield objects (via `_reset_objects`) THEN applies effects in layer/timestamp order. `apply_all` and `remove_expired` are ONLY called in `_do_cleanup_step` (turn.py:138-141) — not by SBAs or events.\n   - CardImpl._reset_characteristics resets card_types→_original_card_types and keywords→_original_keywords. Creature._reset_characteristics also resets modified_power/toughness/counters + combat flags. `Creature.power = modified_power + plus_one_counters - minus_one_counters`.\n   - Gap H: run_turn (turn.py:199-208) — if active player `_turns_to_skip > 0`, decrement and `advance_phase()` until turn_number changes, return (skips whole turn).\n   - DeterministicPlayer (engine/player.py): choose/choose_target/choose_yes_no/choose_card/assign_damage_order all pop from `_script` deque; `remaining_choices`; ScriptExhaustedError when empty.\n   - test_utils: create_game(deck1,deck2,scripts=...) (active_player_index=0/p1, life 20, empty libs reset drawn_from_empty flag). set_board_state(game, idx, battlefield=/hand=/graveyard=/life=/mana={ManaType:amt}). cast_spell appendlefts targets reversed. declare_attackers appendlefts the attackers list itself. Stack has no `size()` — use `len(game.stack._items)`.\n   - discard(game, player, card) (engine.game). move_to_zone(game, card, from_zone, to_zone) (engine.zones).\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_13/card_impl.py` — DONE. `class EmeritusOfTruceSwordsToPlowshares(Creature)` (class name kept from template). {1}{W}{W} (ManaCost.parse can't handle \"//\"; hard-coded creature side), 3/3, subtypes {\"Cat\",\"Cleric\"}, keywords Keyword(0), `self.colors = {Color.WHITE}`, `self.prepared = False`. Module helpers `_count_creatures(game, player)`, `_all_creatures(game)`. `get_targets` returns one player TargetRequirement (`hasattr(obj,\"life\")`). `register_triggers` registers EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent (condition `e.permanent is source`); effect resolves token target from chosen_targets[0]/_resolve_target/default ctrl, creates Inkling Creature (1/1, FLYING, subtypes {\"Inkling\"}, `token.colors = {Color.WHITE, Color.BLACK}`) via create_token, then sets `prepared=True` if any opponent's creature count > controller's. `cast_swords_copy(game, target_creature)`: reads power+controller, move_to_zone BATTLEFIELD→EXILE, controller gains life=power, sets prepared=False. `get_activated_abilities()` returns [] unless prepared, else one ActivatedAbility (cost pays {W}, effect choose_card among _all_creatures then cast_swords_copy).\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_13/tests.py` — DONE, 9 tests pass (TestProperties, TestEnters x4, TestPrepared x2, TestSwords x2). Uses manual `fire_event(EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent(...))` + `_resolve_stack` pattern; activated-ability test wraps in ActivatedAbilityInstance + activate_ability.\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_97/card_impl.py` — DONE. `class RalZarekGuestLecturer(Planeswalker)` {1}{B}{B}, starting_loyalty=3, supertypes {Supertype.LEGENDARY}, subtypes {\"Ral\"}, `self.colors = {Color.BLACK}`. Helper `_get_single_target(pw)` (chosen_targets[0] or _resolve_target). `get_loyalty_abilities()` returns 4 LoyaltyAbility in order [+1, -1, -2, -7]: +1 surveil 2 (look at top 2 via `library.top(2)`, process top-first, choose_yes_no→graveyard else keep on top); -1 iterate `chosen_targets` (player list, tolerate empty), each non-empty-hand player choose_card then discard; -2 reanimate single target if creature card in controller graveyard with cmc≤3 → move_to_zone GRAVEYARD→BATTLEFIELD (sets card.controller=ctrl first); -7 flip 5 coins via `ctrl.choose_yes_no(\"Flip a coin — heads?\")`, heads count = X, opponent (chosen_targets[0] or other player) `_turns_to_skip += X`.\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py` — DONE, 15 tests pass. Helper `_abilities(ral)` returns dict keyed by loyalty_cost; `_set_library(player, cards_bottom_to_top)`. Includes a `run_turn` Gap-H skip integration test (`test_skip_counter_consumed_by_run_turn`: set active idx 0, p1._turns_to_skip=1, run_turn, assert decremented to 0 and turn_number==start+1).\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_257/card_impl.py` — JUST WRITTEN (tests NOT yet written/run). `class GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex(Land)`. __init__ sets creature-capable attrs (base_power=0, base_toughness=0, modified_power=0, modified_toughness=0, plus_one/minus_one_counters=0, _base_plus_one/minus_one_counters=0, damage_marked=0, summoning_sick=False, is_attacking=False, is_blocking=False, dealt_deathtouch_damage=False, _animated=False, _pump_registered=False). Has `power`/`toughness` properties (modified + counters). Overrides `_reset_characteristics`: super() then if `_animated` re-adds CREATURE+Wizard, then resets modified_power/toughness=base, counters=_base. `get_mana_abilities()` returns 2 ManaAbility: ({T}: Add {C}) tap→add COLORLESS; ({T}, Pay 1 life: any color) cost taps+`ctrl.life -= 1`, effect `ctrl.choose(_ANY_COLORS,...)` then add chosen color (default WHITE). `get_activated_abilities()` returns one {5} animation ActivatedAbility: cost guards `not _animated and CREATURE not in card_types`, pays ManaCost.parse(\"{5}\"); effect calls `self.animate(game)`. `animate(game)`: guarded idempotent — sets _animated=True, card_types|={CREATURE}, subtypes|={\"Wizard\"}, base/modified P/T=2/4, summoning_sick=False, calls `_register_pump_trigger`. `_register_pump_trigger`: guarded by _pump_registered; registers SpellCastTriggeredEvent (condition: `e.controller is ctrl` AND spell card_types & {INSTANT,SORCERY}), effect `source.modified_power += 1`. Module constants `_INSTANT_SORCERY={CardType.INSTANT,CardType.SORCERY}`, `_ANY_COLORS=[WHITE,BLUE,BLACK,RED,GREEN]`, `_ANIMATE_COST=\"{5}\"`. Docstring documents: animation durability via _reset_characteristics override; pump is direct transient modified_power bump wiped at cleanup apply_all; any-color \"I/S only\" restriction NOT enforced (mana untagged).\n   - `/workspace/engine/basic_lands.py` — read as analogue for ManaAbility (`_tap_cost(game, source)->bool`, effect `controller.mana_pool.add(ManaType.X, 1)`).\n   - `/workspace/cards/fdn/fdn_136/card_impl.py` (Angel of Finality) — read; self-ETB via register_triggers + condition `event.permanent is source`, reads target via `chosen_targets`/`_resolve_target`.\n   - `/workspace/cards/fdn/fdn_134/card_impl.py` (Ajani) — read; LoyaltyAbility structure, reads `pw._resolve_target`.\n   - `/workspace/cards/fdn/fdn_24/card_impl.py` (Squad Rallier) — read; get_activated_abilities returns [ActivatedAbility(cost=_cost(game,src)->bool, effect=_effect(game)->None, description)]; note their colored ability cost approximated as generic, but ManaPool.can_pay handles colored pips properly.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered in this session. sos_13 (9 tests) and sos_97 (15 tests) passed on first run; engine suites stayed green (1154, then 1160 passed). The earlier-session harness rule \"must Read template before Write\" was respected for all three cards (read template first each time).\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - sos_13: Reconciled the apparent contradiction about self-ETB triggers by reading move_to_zone — confirmed register_triggers runs BEFORE ETB fires for normally-resolved permanents (so Angel-of-Finality-style self-ETB works), unlike create_token. Chose the register_triggers + EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent pattern. Modeled \"Prepared\" (non-Keyword) as `self.prepared` boolean and \"cast a copy of Swords to Plowshares\" as an activated ability + a directly-callable `cast_swords_copy` method.\n   - sos_97: Modeled coin flips deterministically via choose_yes_no (testable). Implemented surveil 2 by popping top 2, processing top-first, keeping declined cards back on top. Confirmed Gap H `_turns_to_skip` is consumed in run_turn.\n   - sos_257: Designed animation durability via overriding `_reset_characteristics` (PLAN-endorsed \"Simpler\" path) rather than registering a TYPE continuous effect. Pump (+1/+0 EOT) implemented as a direct `modified_power += 1` bump (transient), relying on cleanup's apply_all→_reset_characteristics to wipe it back to base 2/4. Verified apply_all is only called at cleanup so the bump persists until then. Set base_power/base_toughness=2/4 on animation so _reset_characteristics restores 2/4.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - (Opening of this continuation): system-reminders showing Read results for sos_201/tests.py, sos_201/card_impl.py, sos_120/tests.py, sos_120/card_impl.py, s